 key="edge_source_id">S07</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S07_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">If so, the Base Score increases and the Confidentiality, Integrity and Authentication metrics should be scored relative to the impacted component</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be scored</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be scored", "be scoring"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_057830cb2e36f750" source="e_c4631f903e1159e5" target="e_c7bbd6f495adf548"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be managed by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f81d3c8494e829f1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S07</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S07_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">An exploited vulnerability can only affect resources managed by the same security authority</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be managed by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be managed by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_b14badf400001ec5" source="e_0651ca14b1e582f2" target="e_41977bbb956fd210"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are same In</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_211a8b64a8ea1d98</data><data key="edge_source_id">S07</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S07_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In this case, the vulnerable component and the impacted component are either the same, or both are managed by the same security authority</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are same In</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are same In"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_66f18569d154491f" source="e_26e0466f06957bd3" target="e_41977bbb956fd210"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are same In</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6d3c2dd76299347e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S07</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S07_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In this case, the vulnerable component and the impacted component are either the same, or both are managed by the same security authority</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are same In</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are same In"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_643cdc1501f832f5" source="e_22d8a27b5ffe2dfd" target="e_c7bbd6f495adf548"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are managed by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d95c557bfa3bd512</data><data key="edge_source_id">S07</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S07_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In this case, the vulnerable component and the impacted component are either the same, or both are managed by the same security authority</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are managed by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are managed by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_93e3d728b6260345" source="e_841d5cae83210039" target="e_c1b8569aebaf6353"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be managed by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f4e35183bbeebc24</data><data key="edge_source_id">S07</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S07_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This metric measures the impact to the confidentiality of the information resources managed by a software component due to a successfully exploited vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be managed by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be managed by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_ef21dde8c89d1731" source="e_fabb36a448bb30b7" target="e_eb1797b298a230c0"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">disclosed</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f4681b77310d5a73</data><data key="edge_source_id">S07</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S07_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Alternatively, access to only some restricted information is obtained, but the disclosed information presents a direct, serious impact</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">disclosed</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["disclosed"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_660b0bf8b3e97226" source="e_d2b630e61129d09b" target="e_26e0466f06957bd3"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be protected by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3fbe1d435b4350c1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S07</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S07_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, the attacker is able to modify any/all files protected by the impacted component</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be protected by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be protected by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_93754f8fc27b735e" source="e_332fd4a216e1c401" target="e_2228b2b192c550b5"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be resulting from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4944ac91949c0697</data><data key="edge_source_id">S07</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S07_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This metric measures the impact to the availability of the impacted component resulting from a successfully exploited vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be resulting from</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be resulting from"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_48b2af474c3b01ea" source="e_e56e3d4771ca46d9" target="e_841d5cae83210039"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">refers to accessibility of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ef94ad81a19dbc7c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S07</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S07_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Since availability refers to the accessibility of information resources, attacks that consume network bandwidth, processor cycles, or disk space all impact the availability of an impacted component</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">refers to accessibility of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["refers to accessibility of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_4053b6bcea62daf7" source="e_e56e3d4771ca46d9" target="e_bf0bee0969a73481"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">refers to accessibility of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0322c29a9a0f46d2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S07</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S07_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Since availability refers to the accessibility of information resources, attacks that consume network bandwidth, processor cycles, or disk space all impact the availability of an impacted component</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">refers to accessibility of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["refers to accessibility of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_5e25b82ff9f96e84" source="e_e56e3d4771ca46d9" target="e_d37e8eb9896152d1"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">refers to accessibility of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4c3b403fc73e0d05</data><data key="edge_source_id">S07</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S07_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Since availability refers to the accessibility of information resources, attacks that consume network bandwidth, processor cycles, or disk space all impact the availability of an impacted component</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">refers to accessibility of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["refers to accessibility of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_f8cd6ea2d9802186" source="e_22e800482ee5b5fd" target="e_4058f076b2d4719d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">consume</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_dd278ed009449947</data><data key="edge_source_id">S07</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S07_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Since availability refers to the accessibility of information resources, attacks that consume network bandwidth, processor cycles, or disk space all impact the availability of an impacted component</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">consume</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["consume"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_ceadb59a64de1adb" source="e_527c56c7674a26dd" target="e_904da0b4f3960fb3"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is important factor for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2baa48363ac62fab</data><data key="edge_source_id">S07</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S07_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Remediation Level of a vulnerability is an important factor for prioritization</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is important factor for</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is important factor for"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_19da5781436f636a" source="e_4228490cbf8a6d91" target="e_98c110f1e21aa4eb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is unpatched when</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_76ba38aa28f5ab21</data><data key="edge_source_id">S07</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S07_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The typical vulnerability is unpatched when initially published</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is unpatched when</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is unpatched when"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_da401d512c9c179a" source="e_edf56b768b8904e2" target="e_a568574ebde0ab4b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">becomes</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_15373b5a45a779d5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S07</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S07_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Each of these respective stages adjusts the temporal score downwards, reflecting the decreasing urgency as remediation becomes final</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">becomes</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["becomes", "has become"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_b67c119a92361861" source="e_298a9593b67b7b1f" target="e_34cf20183f45e324"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has issued</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e0389d3906ac4fad</data><data key="edge_source_id">S07</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S07_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Either the vendor has issued an official patch, or an upgrade is available</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">has issued</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["has issued"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_1f4ab3539842c39f" source="e_298a9593b67b7b1f" target="e_d068a0aa82ac3043"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has issued</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8f1b31a07439e543</data><data key="edge_source_id">S07</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S07_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Either the vendor has issued an official patch, or an upgrade is available</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">has issued</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["has issued"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_1d93c212e4ec370c" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_cf4606d100a09d0c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is known to exist with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_acd8eaaffb0276e9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S07</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S07_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The urgency of a vulnerability is higher when a vulnerability is known to exist with certainty</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is known to exist with</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is known to exist with"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_475b827260d54088" source="e_4676679afd99eed0" target="e_3655237b10b88be1"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">suggests</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_262ccbb686f6387e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S07</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S07_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This metric also suggests the level of technical knowledge available to would-be attackers</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">suggests</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["suggests"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_26d77920cd448b66" source="e_556b627b7c43e3ef" target="e_9ffb7cbec78fa95f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">do use</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e1ffa661f34fc3b8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S07</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S07_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Block inbound traffic on UDP ports 500 and 4500 for systems that do not use IKE</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">use</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["use", "uses", "do use", "Uses"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_483f4a114e1af4ba" source="e_5d5372b986026500" target="e_5ed1bb6674bf66cb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be allow inbound traffic on UDP ports only from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_168f662659868e91</data><data key="edge_source_id">S07</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S07_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For systems that require IKE, configure firewall rules to allow inbound traffic on UDP ports 500 and 4500 only from known peer addresses</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be allow inbound traffic on UDP ports only from</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be allow inbound traffic on UDP ports only from"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_a2a3929e179c74af" source="e_0e94d80f0d0a20ab" target="e_cd02294221b23956"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">do replace</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_19c0f4af0d1da3b6</data><data key="edge_source_id">S07</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S07_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">These actions reduce the attack surface but do not replace installing the security update</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">do replace</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["do replace"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_16a1d3b3eb38c7cd" source="e_e34c73ce7cdf1ddd" target="e_a05dbb2f9eacc462"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">send crafted packets to Windows machine with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_bc46b9584d9a47da</data><data key="edge_source_id">S07</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S07_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">An unauthenticated attacker could send specially crafted packets to a Windows machine with Internet Key Exchange (IKE) version 2 enabled, which could enable remote code execution</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">send crafted packets to Windows machine with</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["send crafted packets to Windows machine with"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_4de00a3e65a3d071" source="e_e34c73ce7cdf1ddd" target="e_666e09d333cc307c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">send</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b7b7b362d04d0353</data><data key="edge_source_id">S07</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S07_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">An unauthenticated attacker could send specially crafted packets to a Windows machine with Internet Key Exchange (IKE) version 2 enabled, which could enable remote code execution</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">send</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["send", "sends"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_5b0aa2712ca32cb9" source="e_b82be424e7d21f94" target="e_a7523256c9515f68"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">enable</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7035b8aebf3f79b8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S07</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S07_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">An unauthenticated attacker could send specially crafted packets to a Windows machine with Internet Key Exchange (IKE) version 2 enabled, which could enable remote code execution</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">enable</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["enable"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_0aeaa7b773a304b1" source="e_a1dcdd289f57b065" target="e_15c6d0b1e60c9c9a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">protect customers through</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_68310d5a9f511284</data><data key="edge_source_id">S07</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S07_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Microsoft recognizes the efforts of those in the security community who help us protect customers through coordinated vulnerability disclosure</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">protect customers through</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["protect customers through"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_3c7b023bea833793" source="e_8e81ce852cc92461" target="e_84268809b8f931f7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">recognizes</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_db32464e74b47bc2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S07</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S07_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Microsoft recognizes the efforts of those in the security community who help us protect customers through coordinated vulnerability disclosure</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">recognizes</data><data key="edge_domain">Vendor</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["recognizes"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_b23227aeb4f6e99d" source="e_5c980ac08d8e06db" target="e_422ecd83d8fd548b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_36ea1328e61fd351</data><data key="edge_source_id">S07</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S07_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">How satisfied are you with the MSRC Security Update Guide?</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are with</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are with"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_3dabf531d9ef5538" source="e_056762b3f0d13b70" target="e_2da887c9a54f6ac7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be affecting</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_289fb4b2b54da985</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">On July 14, 2026, Rapid7 and Microsoft disclosed CVE-2026-55040, an authentication bypass vulnerability affecting Microsoft SharePoint</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be affecting</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Organization</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be affecting"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_916424803487076d" source="e_7b01f3c127e786ab" target="e_4a68b44291d658d4"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is based upon</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_18f3ea45f592da53</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The below analysis is based upon decompilation and code review of the Microsoft.SharePoint.IdentityModel module from a fully patched SharePoint Server Subscription Edition instance</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is based upon</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Product</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is based upon"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_a4c270fbc51a5fff" source="e_7b01f3c127e786ab" target="e_49f13115e9ff0ecd"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is based upon</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_68ff924a6708c009</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The below analysis is based upon decompilation and code review of the Microsoft.SharePoint.IdentityModel module from a fully patched SharePoint Server Subscription Edition instance</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is based upon</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is based upon"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_aa0e9610f35b39fa" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_c5709770f6576cc4"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">resides in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b8ca7e8e2afd9fd3</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The vulnerability resides in the SPJsonWebSecurityTokenHandlerV2 class and its base class SPJsonWebSecurityBaseTokenHandlerV2, which together implement the token parsing and validation logic for Bearer service-to-service (S2S) tokens</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">resides in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["resides in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_ae301f243dfd5c47" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_5e915c1a4e957b7b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">resides in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4711bedc7b87c3b8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The vulnerability resides in the SPJsonWebSecurityTokenHandlerV2 class and its base class SPJsonWebSecurityBaseTokenHandlerV2, which together implement the token parsing and validation logic for Bearer service-to-service (S2S) tokens</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">resides in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["resides in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_5c3c880ef5fd83e0" source="e_c5709770f6576cc4" target="e_c14cac9c7ee8b541"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">implement token parsing for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_175d65eb69401dda</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The vulnerability resides in the SPJsonWebSecurityTokenHandlerV2 class and its base class SPJsonWebSecurityBaseTokenHandlerV2, which together implement the token parsing and validation logic for Bearer service-to-service (S2S) tokens</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">implement token parsing for</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["implement token parsing for"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_3350aa0d28b5b167" source="e_c5709770f6576cc4" target="e_71ac8e151b57b1d9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">implement</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_54763ee546625597</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The vulnerability resides in the SPJsonWebSecurityTokenHandlerV2 class and its base class SPJsonWebSecurityBaseTokenHandlerV2, which together implement the token parsing and validation logic for Bearer service-to-service (S2S) tokens</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">implement</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["implement", "implements"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_55c7346363ab996f" source="e_5e915c1a4e957b7b" target="e_c14cac9c7ee8b541"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">implement token parsing for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c450099b8bdb2287</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The vulnerability resides in the SPJsonWebSecurityTokenHandlerV2 class and its base class SPJsonWebSecurityBaseTokenHandlerV2, which together implement the token parsing and validation logic for Bearer service-to-service (S2S) tokens</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">implement token parsing for</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["implement token parsing for"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_5d217982f2bbec44" source="e_5e915c1a4e957b7b" target="e_71ac8e151b57b1d9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">implement</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ab4aff3bb4f102cc</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The vulnerability resides in the SPJsonWebSecurityTokenHandlerV2 class and its base class SPJsonWebSecurityBaseTokenHandlerV2, which together implement the token parsing and validation logic for Bearer service-to-service (S2S) tokens</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">implement</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["implement", "implements"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_c5b21b5a7ee1d6ab" source="e_c5bc2eee5a4027b0" target="e_029f7bbb28bce08c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">uses</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d66d2e148c009ab1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">SharePoint's S2S authentication uses a nested JWT structure: an outer token containing user identity claims, and an inner "actor token" embedded in the actortoken claim</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">use</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["use", "uses", "do use", "Uses"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_05d4cccbada896fe" source="e_8c2e65be6661f517" target="e_137cb2a8e14bd3d8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be signed by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ad0110502d11d389</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The actor token represents the calling application and is expected to be cryptographically signed by a trusted certificate</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be signed by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be signed by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_6101feb72a6534db" source="e_b82be424e7d21f94" target="e_de0c3d287c57fa3e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">extracts Bearer token from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_78e2c7d22e1132d3</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The validation flow begins in SPApplicationAuthenticationModuleV2.TryExtractAndValidateToken(), which extracts the Bearer token from the Authorization header, parses it via SPJsonWebSecurityBaseTokenHandlerV2.ReadToken(), and then validates it via SPJsonWebSecurityTokenHandlerV2.ValidateToken()</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">extracts Bearer token from</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["extracts Bearer token from"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_535b110dabaca421" source="e_50269ab6fd8fff23" target="e_6552561d836c55d3"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">stack</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_05c3d0f9397ddbd3</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The debugger call stack below shows the call stack at the time of calling ValidateToken</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">stack</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["stack"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_d03c4b9c1ce5b5da" source="e_78fa85289ca7d809" target="e_d8d85d45361688ea"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is System.Web.HttpApplication httpApplication out</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b37d99edce40fcd5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Microsoft.SharePoint.IdentityModel.dll!Microsoft.SharePoint.IdentityModel.SPApplicationAuthenticationModuleV2.ConstructIClaimsPrincipalAndSetThreadIdentity(System.Web.HttpApplication httpApplication, System.Web.HttpContext httpContext, Microsoft.SharePoint.IdentityModel.SPFederationAuthenticationModuleV2 fam, out string tokenType) (IL≈0x0041, Native=0x00007FFC730A