ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">- Attacker sends a JWT with alg: none in the outer header, so no signature is required in the outer token</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">sends JWT with</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["sends JWT with"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_4c4e952e06c52cac" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_6d3a01919cc8a376"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">sends</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7491a09a8bd9ab34</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">- Attacker sends a JWT with alg: none in the outer header, so no signature is required in the outer token</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">send</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["send", "sends"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_70a663da6d396cc4" source="e_0d2194283fb10c7e" target="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">Name</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1fce9228039a8093</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">After validation, the outer token's nameid claim, containing either an attacker controlled Windows Security Identifier (SID) or an attacker controlled User Principal Name (UPN), is resolved to a user identity via SPIncomingServerToServerProtocolIdentityHandlerV2.ValidateAndEnsureIdentity()</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">Name</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["Name"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_b7fa3069fd6a29ae" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_d605a1c83e9a76e2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">see</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_35f83d98dd0d3fc6</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">We can see a concrete example of the bypass in action by inspecting the HTTP requests required to achieve the authentication bypass</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">see</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["see"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_06031074ee9ed543" source="e_697bbe8ca55c5f82" target="e_1bb0bfedc1e44926"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be required to achieve</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8aaefbd5f6c588e9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">We can see a concrete example of the bypass in action by inspecting the HTTP requests required to achieve the authentication bypass</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be required to achieve</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be required to achieve"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_57949d04874710ac" source="e_de4f2aa066892746" target="e_4d349aae7d59df71"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be use in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_46f4c3da13342a08</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In order to know the x5t value to use in the inner actortoken token, we must first retrieve the x509 certificate of the STS signing certificate from the target SharePoint site</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be use in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be use in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_6ac02a2e7d487a99" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_6620f7434e7041fd"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">compute</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d1f59856bfa0f25e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Using the above x509 certificate, we can compute the x5t by base64 decoding the entire x509 certificate, computing the SHA1 digest value, then base64 encoding that raw digest value</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">compute</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["compute"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_85c7b1c2ac2c8a4d" source="e_35400971c008bd74" target="e_47869b8b12d1452e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">digest</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a595f1675dd17ebe</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Using the above x509 certificate, we can compute the x5t by base64 decoding the entire x509 certificate, computing the SHA1 digest value, then base64 encoding that raw digest value</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">digest</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["digest"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_c3e353f0fa599abc" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_dec97ba9f61bcb68"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">use</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ee2264ae8b1b8799</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">We can also see we discover the target realm (af90cc03-4a26-45e9-906a-609cebcebbde) which we will use later in the forged JWT</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">use</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["use", "uses", "do use", "Uses"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_aa92c711eb36b615" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_cec174574715ef69"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">begin to construct</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_177487bc0a4e590e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">We then begin to construct the malicious JWT</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">begin to construct</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["begin to construct"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_466630eeb9b30b27" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_e41dcba38a6a6f27"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">identify in example</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2817d311ffb01243</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Name ID (nameid) represent the SharePoint user we will identify as, in our example we use a SID of S-1-5-21-4203888158-2793536450-3921675298-500 which represent the domain admin that we want to authenticate as using the urn:office:idp:activedirectory identity provider</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">identify in example</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["identify in example"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_32def83f907a1948" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_e41dcba38a6a6f27"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">identify</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b90bbd0ea753307b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Name ID (nameid) represent the SharePoint user we will identify as, in our example we use a SID of S-1-5-21-4203888158-2793536450-3921675298-500 which represent the domain admin that we want to authenticate as using the urn:office:idp:activedirectory identity provider</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">identifies</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["identifies", "identify"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_b59fe491404b7fbf" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_509e3f0c8e4c334a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">use</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6137401d88824710</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Name ID (nameid) represent the SharePoint user we will identify as, in our example we use a SID of S-1-5-21-4203888158-2793536450-3921675298-500 which represent the domain admin that we want to authenticate as using the urn:office:idp:activedirectory identity provider</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">use</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["use", "uses", "do use", "Uses"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_94ddca69c0d59e3a" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_c8716b40e55a7d2d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">authenticate as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_66895463b66f4cf5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Name ID (nameid) represent the SharePoint user we will identify as, in our example we use a SID of S-1-5-21-4203888158-2793536450-3921675298-500 which represent the domain admin that we want to authenticate as using the urn:office:idp:activedirectory identity provider</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">authenticate as</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["authenticate as"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_8f8d29bbc16d3821" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_563b55c70c68fe59"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">use</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a9416bf10b8b1eb5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">We can use an SMB NULL session to query the LSARPC named pipe and learn the domain's Domain ID value</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">use</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["use", "uses", "do use", "Uses"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_8c98e8e3b8d7e3d8" source="e_3da4c5809c640a71" target="e_4e60eea811eef52e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is more</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8457008bbeae2c2e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">However, discovering a valid SID is more reliable in an automated scenario (assuming you can access the domain controller) than brute forcing potential UPN's, which is best suited to manual reconnaissance</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is more</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is more"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_62cba2382762e6e3" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_32bf088eb1f5140a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">have header</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_efa6fa7a16221372</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Inspecting the inner actortoken token, it will have a header as shown below, which includes the x5t value i_gz5qfYp5YPWAK1__0YhZnipLI corresponding to the SharePoint server's STS signing certificate</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">have header</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["have header"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_059a07e854c6a133" source="e_e163460c91338b08" target="e_8264f38f98ed0f54"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">allows call to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2882bb725835a0b9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C11</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Note the nameid of this token is the same as the issuer of the STS certificate, this allows a call to SPJsonWebSecurityBaseTokenHandlerV2.ValidateActorIsSelfIssuer to succeed</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">allows call to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["allows call to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_0c1d6cc9594f964e" source="e_e163460c91338b08" target="e_9329b224df96eb01"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">allows call to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_14c1ee61397bd893</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C11</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Note the nameid of this token is the same as the issuer of the STS certificate, this allows a call to SPJsonWebSecurityBaseTokenHandlerV2.ValidateActorIsSelfIssuer to succeed</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">allows call to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["allows call to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_63ea4127e4609c74" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_6d930bf9f79f5d74"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be Constructing</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_90c20026775bf646</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C11</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Constructing the above JWT, we can base64 encode it as a bearer token and make a request to an authenticated endpoint, such as /_api/web/currentuser and prove we are authenticating as a SharePoint user</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be Constructing</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be Constructing"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_4c1249a650e960e3" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_262dca47d4b181dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">base64</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_922241cc9b53bb92</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C11</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Constructing the above JWT, we can base64 encode it as a bearer token and make a request to an authenticated endpoint, such as /_api/web/currentuser and prove we are authenticating as a SharePoint user</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">base64</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["base64"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_caccfc74f3b63b74" source="e_1e7e8c1028226135" target="e_2da887c9a54f6ac7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be affecting</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ad7734dbd91a685e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">On August 11, 2026, Rapid7 and Microsoft disclosed CVE-2026-63520, a remote code execution (RCE) vulnerability affecting Microsoft SharePoint</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be affecting</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Organization</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be affecting"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_92def04fd8e88f51" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_82b91fdd0e399842"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">have exploited issue by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9c791c96742ebfbf</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When comparing the two analysis of CVE-2026-63520, we can see how we have exploited the issue by leveraging a Database Line-of-Business (LOB) system and an ObjectDataProvider based gadget chain, whilst the VulnCheck analysis has exploited the issue by leveraging a DotNetAssembly LOB system and a LosFormatter based gadget chain</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">has exploited issue by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["has exploited issue by", "have exploited issue by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_6b1cbbf03a45277f" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_11f46ecc3d6429b6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">have exploited issue by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4e4e92f2c863f662</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When comparing the two analysis of CVE-2026-63520, we can see how we have exploited the issue by leveraging a Database Line-of-Business (LOB) system and an ObjectDataProvider based gadget chain, whilst the VulnCheck analysis has exploited the issue by leveraging a DotNetAssembly LOB system and a LosFormatter based gadget chain</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">has exploited issue by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["has exploited issue by", "have exploited issue by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_09692f741f530083" source="e_4e650f44977b3e60" target="e_7b90f8e055178aed"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has exploited issue by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_26c07c81dc019dd5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When comparing the two analysis of CVE-2026-63520, we can see how we have exploited the issue by leveraging a Database Line-of-Business (LOB) system and an ObjectDataProvider based gadget chain, whilst the VulnCheck analysis has exploited the issue by leveraging a DotNetAssembly LOB system and a LosFormatter based gadget chain</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">has exploited issue by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["has exploited issue by", "have exploited issue by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_97be6e64c4aa7375" source="e_4e650f44977b3e60" target="e_837e5805db9952ca"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has exploited issue by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_88c3fe9ad1311f86</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When comparing the two analysis of CVE-2026-63520, we can see how we have exploited the issue by leveraging a Database Line-of-Business (LOB) system and an ObjectDataProvider based gadget chain, whilst the VulnCheck analysis has exploited the issue by leveraging a DotNetAssembly LOB system and a LosFormatter based gadget chain</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">has exploited issue by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["has exploited issue by", "have exploited issue by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_360268a1c55b7203" source="e_086aa5bfb79357b0" target="e_e163460c91338b08"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">account for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_04fb86e1f125279d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Defenders should account for this when detecting CVE-2026-63520</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">account for</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["account for", "accounts for"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_77129be2be37445a" source="e_e163460c91338b08" target="e_ae8d6edb17b6529d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is due to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a3e5e27749ebd9dc</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This is due to an unrestricted .NET type instantiation and property-setting primitive in the DbTypeReflector class, which resolves arbitrary assembly-qualified type names from BDC model XML without any allowlist or safety enforcement</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is due to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is due to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_7788a10fbf96b139" source="e_985cab375dab17b5" target="e_334e3fd559093d72"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">resolves arbitrary assembly-qualified type names from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_56a75e18bd0a7d80</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This is due to an unrestricted .NET type instantiation and property-setting primitive in the DbTypeReflector class, which resolves arbitrary assembly-qualified type names from BDC model XML without any allowlist or safety enforcement</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">resolves arbitrary assembly-qualified type names from</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["resolves arbitrary assembly-qualified type names from"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_f6f6739af062be42" source="e_985cab375dab17b5" target="e_4139f702e143b880"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">resolves arbitrary assembly-qualified type names without</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c25086b19cbdb394</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This is due to an unrestricted .NET type instantiation and property-setting primitive in the DbTypeReflector class, which resolves arbitrary assembly-qualified type names from BDC model XML without any allowlist or safety enforcement</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">resolves arbitrary assembly-qualified type names without</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["resolves arbitrary assembly-qualified type names without"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_a7f33dba0871b324" source="e_985cab375dab17b5" target="e_904eea2c6691ab9e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">resolves</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d0bade8f52f8918e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This is due to an unrestricted .NET type instantiation and property-setting primitive in the DbTypeReflector class, which resolves arbitrary assembly-qualified type names from BDC model XML without any allowlist or safety enforcement</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">resolves</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["resolves"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_abbfc9a238ecb6d4" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_16481add93a0689f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">upload</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_dfc1322701b26be0</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">An attacker who can upload a malicious .bdcm model file and trigger entity execution can instantiate any .NET type available in the Global Assembly Cache (GAC), set arbitrary properties on those instances, and leverage property-setter side-effects to achieve OS command execution</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">upload</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["upload"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_b3ba991e16050f0a" source="e_5c77927661666bef" target="e_c5dfb8860a56c364"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be achieve</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a21ef53dba8647d5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">An attacker who can upload a malicious .bdcm model file and trigger entity execution can instantiate any .NET type available in the Global Assembly Cache (GAC), set arbitrary properties on those instances, and leverage property-setter side-effects to achieve OS command execution</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be achieve</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be achieve"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_75c7e9ffd7a57c50" source="e_71704402a2035bf7" target="e_c5dfb8860a56c364"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be achieve</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2ad07dceeb9f80fa</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">An attacker who can upload a malicious .bdcm model file and trigger entity execution can instantiate any .NET type available in the Global Assembly Cache (GAC), set arbitrary properties on those instances, and leverage property-setter side-effects to achieve OS command execution</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be achieve</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be achieve"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_fdd476362f9b17ef" source="e_db0111d55cfc1e1f" target="e_3ecd9f953ff0df40"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be set arbitrary properties on</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7cc03c23eb13fdb7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">An attacker who can upload a malicious .bdcm model file and trigger entity execution can instantiate any .NET type available in the Global Assembly Cache (GAC), set arbitrary properties on those instances, and leverage property-setter side-effects to achieve OS command execution</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be set arbitrary properties on</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be set arbitrary properties on"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_62eb08f1ced3e4fd" source="e_71704402a2035bf7" target="e_3ecd9f953ff0df40"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be set arbitrary properties on</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e6efd5d3ed6ab7ea</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">An attacker who can upload a malicious .bdcm model file and trigger entity execution can instantiate any .NET type available in the Global Assembly Cache (GAC), set arbitrary properties on those instances, and leverage property-setter side-effects to achieve OS command execution</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be set arbitrary properties on</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be set arbitrary properties on"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_467bc0737b4fb1c1" source="e_0dd1994901856e68" target="e_5004a250dc4e7fbc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">was helpful when</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_087942dee46ab91b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Note that there is prior work in this space that was very helpful when conducting this research</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">was helpful when</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["was helpful when"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_44300a60f1b020fe" source="e_fa57f6906d6bad6d" target="e_2d31e1284f8f402d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">discusses leveraging BDC models for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1f80c870151d49d3</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The writeup of CVE-2019-1257 by the ZDI research team discusses leveraging BDC models for unsafe .NET type instantiation</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">discusses leveraging BDC models for</data><data key="edge_domain">CVE</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["discusses leveraging BDC models for"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_f684e234dec93a03" source="e_56b6e04e82934e27" target="e_b18d3845b358d980"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">uses type reflectors to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_95e3302a6b2ebab8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The BDC subsystem uses "type reflectors" to resolve .NET types from the TypeName attribute of TypeDescriptor elements in BDC model XML</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">uses type reflectors to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["uses type reflectors to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_d4bcc0b91e322928" source="e_56b6e04e82934e27" target="e_7aaa7aa6d98b2c67"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">uses</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7a8439ed5ecfca69</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The BDC subsystem uses "type reflectors" to resolve .NET types from the TypeName attribute of TypeDescriptor elements in BDC model XML</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">use</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["use", "uses", "do use", "Uses"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_64eab519596c55f1" source="e_791de43fccfd7f2f" target="e_cb9f5348cc19aca7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">uses</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_59cb102841f1c22e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For Database-type LobSystem definitions, SharePoint uses DbTypeReflector, which inherits from DotNetTypeReflector, as shown below</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">use</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["use", "uses", "do use", "Uses"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_b16e1dcbd5172b36" source="e_cb9f5348cc19aca7" target="e_0f096c4f79bb42fb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">inherits from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_624cf52ce93f1cfe</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For Database-type LobSystem definitions, SharePoint uses DbTypeReflector, which inherits from DotNetTypeReflector, as shown below</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">inherits from</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["inherits from"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_2da2540b9578106a" source="e_200807ea700bfac2" target="e_6f30ccda3c04a8d9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">Text</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d7215c308477c6e8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">&lt;Property Name="RdbCommandType" Type="System.String"&gt;Text&lt;/Property&gt;</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">Text</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["Text"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_a53d240a1b37e6be" source="e_50ec225c8fa75ab5" target="e_ec9024fb051cf8fa"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be observed to execute via tool like</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_906f137c74a416b5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For testing purposes we favor a simple binary like notepad.exe which can easily be observed to execute via a tool like Process Explorer, as shown below in Figure 1</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be observed to execute via tool like</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be observed to execute via tool like"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_aa02927fbf4a6490" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_7761c777d1473a9a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">set CreateNoWindow to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ce3a751237c56585</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">We set CreateNoWindow to true, as the target w3wp.exe IIS worker process is running in Session 0, so will have no desktop attached for displaying window forms</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">set CreateNoWindow to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["set CreateNoWindow to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_5fa334963e3a3f5e" source="e_697bbe8ca55c5f82" target="e_2d31e1284f8f402d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be required to achieve</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9e7104fe3a6e9004</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">We can see a concrete example of the RCE in action by inspecting the HTTP requests required to achieve unsafe .NET type instantiation</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be required to achieve</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be required to achieve"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_9fe4ede88a503b5c" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_992ccb029509eb66"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">see</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_249f536249b5be95</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">We can see a concrete example of the RCE in action by inspecting the HTTP requests required to achieve unsafe .NET type instantiation</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">see</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["see"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_51431b129e29a32d" source="e_1d5a0cdfb1cb9bcf" target="e_1bb0bfedc1e44926"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">have been generated via script for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_bd3a51822ff120fe</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Note that the Bearer authorization token, along with the X-RequestDigest token used in the following requests have been generated via our exploit script for the authentication bypass, CVE-2026-55040</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">have been generated via script for</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["have been generated via script for"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_caca4425cf2a5dd5" source="e_2c7f52ae71073c01" target="e_1bb0bfedc1e44926"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has script for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0465ba882acc9ec2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Note that the Bearer authorization token, along with the X-RequestDigest token used in the following requests have been generated via our exploit script for the authentication bypass, CVE-2026-55040</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">has script for</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["has script for"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_58c1d82a21c4eb73" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_fc7f7e79ce383617"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">upload</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f646102ac17c93c3</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Before we can upload the malicious BDC model, we must first create a BusinessDataMetadataCatalog folder via an HTTP POST request to the /_api/web/folders endpoint</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">upload</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["upload"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_51dfd2ec2f06a28a" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_fc7f7e79ce383617"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">upload</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ba133915ac10ee1a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Next we can upload the malicious BDC model via an HTTP POST request to the /_api/web/GetFolderByServerRelativeUrl endpoint</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">upload</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["upload"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_82d02344880c9e92" source="e_1d65c2006d420154" target="e_4804b2dbd01d82c4"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be calling</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_941d0f5e44f43fee</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C11</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">We trigger unsafe .NET type instantiation via an HTTP POST request to the /_vti_bin/client.svc/ProcessQuery endpoint, calling the FindSpecificDefault method to locate and trigger our malicious gadget chain</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be calling</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be calling"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_e341fe76140a0c2b" source="e_1d65c2006d420154" target="e_80f11a9762cc755f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be calling</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a2f0de542ed53a5b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C11</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">We trigger unsafe .NET type instantiation via an HTTP POST request to the /_vti_bin/client.svc/ProcessQuery endpoint, calling the FindSpecificDefault method to locate and trigger our malicious gadget chain</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be calling</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be calling"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_5c4fb31d5c63bca7" source="e_80f11a9762cc755f" target="e_15a1b8835647268c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be locate</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5851c09bcc234411</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C11</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">We trigger unsafe .NET type instantiation via an HTTP POST request to the /_vti_bin/client.svc/ProcessQuery endpoint, calling the FindSpecificDefault method to locate and trigger our malicious gadget chain</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be locate</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be locate"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_910f7655c743440e" source="e_3ed75ce2898647cc" target="e_4c807bd1aa4450fe"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is object obj out</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d1b66c820e7c3dce</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Microsoft.SharePoint.Client.ServerRuntime.dll!Microsoft.SharePoint.Client.ClientMethodsProcessor.InvokeMethod(object obj, string methodName, System.Xml.XmlNodeList xmlargs, out bool isVoid) (IL≈0x0000, Native=0x00007FFC769A4A50+0x50)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is object obj out</data><data key="edge_domain">Organization</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is object obj out"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_ce6229e7ea6bb6f9" source="e_5c3f7c04d20e26be" target="e_ba9a48b261b71bc9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">published PoC for CVE-2026-55040 on</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0e78b59a4269c584</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Both vulnerabilities were discovered by Rapid7’s Stephen Fewer, who published a PoC for CVE-2026-55040 (the first part of the chain) on August 11</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">published PoC for CVE-2026-55040 on</data><data key="edge_domain">Product</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["published PoC for CVE-2026-55040 on"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_6f3e37c4112a6f9e" source="e_5c3f7c04d20e26be" target="e_8ea2d5e84baadda6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">published PoC for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_22806d37fd4aa9fa</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Both vulnerabilities were discovered by Rapid7’s Stephen Fewer, who published a PoC for CVE-2026-55040 (the first part of the chain) on August 11</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">published PoC for</data><data key="edge_domain">Product</data><data key="edge_range">CVE</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["published PoC for"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_1bd6cda59c76d598" source="e_855a19bc23e9e737" target="e_ed277ba657b8bf3e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">was added to VulnCheck KEV on</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_75395b6919566fa4</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Honeypot providers immediately began reporting exploitation in the wild, and the flaw was added to VulnCheck KEV on August 12 before being added to CISA KEV on August 18</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">was added to VulnCheck KEV on</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["was added to VulnCheck KEV on"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_738489b7ba85b71b" source="e_855a19bc23e9e737" target="e_acd4d41d34c97940"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">was added to VulnCheck KEV before</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_580527f51fe23d6a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Honeypot providers immediately began reporting exploitation in the wild, and the flaw was added to VulnCheck KEV on August 12 before being added to CISA KEV on August 18</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">was added to VulnCheck KEV before</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Product</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["was added to VulnCheck KEV before"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_aa1ed31456357922" source="e_855a19bc23e9e737" target="e_d25c4acdb633e913"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">was added to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_20a4162a1576afe2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Honeypot providers immediately began reporting exploitation in the wild, and the flaw was added to VulnCheck KEV on August 12 before being added to CISA KEV on August 18</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">was added to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["was added to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_2a8780cef8575a86" source="e_a32995c20401aafe" target="e_439cc8762872a084"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">exploit along with version scanner</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_075317b48576605c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As a result, the VulnCheck research team developed a complete RCE