e RCE exploit, along with a version scanner, Suricata and Snort rules, encrypted and unencrypted PCAPs, and ASM queries</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">exploit along with Snort rules</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["exploit along with Snort rules"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_d72f79597063157e" source="e_7f1f6c82d4c24b3a" target="e_6203f55027291b6a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has analysis of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c4d23a5c5bb60e68</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">These artifacts are available to Initial Access Intelligence customers, and the team’s analysis of the SharePoint RCE chain is below</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">has analysis of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["has analysis of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_1934e2205ca89a2d" source="e_5c980ac08d8e06db" target="e_c8dfaccf2a582233"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">use</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2b4f9fc61559ac78</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">You can then use the forged JWT along with the digest value to access the application in “useful” ways, such as to make changes to the application via the Business Connectivity Services (BCS), or more specifically via BDC (Business Data Catalog), the core service on which BCS runs, to achieve RCE</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">use</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["use", "uses", "do use", "Uses"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_b6d0f0facc2d6b94" source="e_10c0749f7978a237" target="e_0a5137e8983f8adf"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be access</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5c7c8ec59da3d8cf</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">You can then use the forged JWT along with the digest value to access the application in “useful” ways, such as to make changes to the application via the Business Connectivity Services (BCS), or more specifically via BDC (Business Data Catalog), the core service on which BCS runs, to achieve RCE</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be access</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be access"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_fe9af94b707d13a6" source="e_10c0749f7978a237" target="e_c5571af9c192ceba"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be access</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6327156810679cc8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">You can then use the forged JWT along with the digest value to access the application in “useful” ways, such as to make changes to the application via the Business Connectivity Services (BCS), or more specifically via BDC (Business Data Catalog), the core service on which BCS runs, to achieve RCE</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be access</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be access"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_a9b1cf721e82f904" source="e_63682437049c7097" target="e_78b456fbfbf7a2f4"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be achieve</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ab79086341148889</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">You can then use the forged JWT along with the digest value to access the application in “useful” ways, such as to make changes to the application via the Business Connectivity Services (BCS), or more specifically via BDC (Business Data Catalog), the core service on which BCS runs, to achieve RCE</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be achieve</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be achieve"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_a84ef81c4b02790a" source="e_6f86ae8844c3ae87" target="e_fbfb70a00355d68e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has disclosure for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_eb11e817803514e1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Rapid7’s disclosure for CVE-2026-63520 describes the issue as unsafe .NET type instantiation within SharePoint’s Business Connectivity Services</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">has disclosure for</data><data key="edge_domain">Organization</data><data key="edge_range">CVE</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["has disclosure for"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_6a82efc01231f96b" source="e_000fbfcccde57e07" target="e_2d31e1284f8f402d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">describes issue as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c86dabaf2ca7cfb6</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Rapid7’s disclosure for CVE-2026-63520 describes the issue as unsafe .NET type instantiation within SharePoint’s Business Connectivity Services</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">describes issue as</data><data key="edge_domain">CVE</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["describes issue as"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_fb314d7cd0cd77e7" source="e_fc7dbd581d39a8a8" target="e_759453b03e46f7eb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">bypass</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_16d9ac90703b4851</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">After reproducing the authentication bypass in our own SharePoint environment, our team diffed KB5002893 to see what changed</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">bypass</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Patch/update</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["bypass"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_e759fbc1a95ece6a" source="e_725367bf832fa264" target="e_b27373d9a9c4626d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be found inside</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_46f034113ba864b0</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The most significant change was a new function, ValidateSafeBcsType, found inside Microsoft.SharePoint/Microsoft/SharePoint/BusinessData/Infrastructure/DotNetTypeReflector.cs</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be found inside</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Organization</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be found inside"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_0d2777b646fda656" source="e_791de43fccfd7f2f" target="e_2f4f3cc513cdd23d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">applies additional validation Starting with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ec18b598e8cf483f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">“Starting with the August 2026 CU, SharePoint applies additional validation to the .NET types that can be used by BCS models</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">applies additional validation Starting with</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["applies additional validation Starting with"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_9749c098692bb3fc" source="e_791de43fccfd7f2f" target="e_2f4f3cc513cdd23d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be Starting with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1a6350e74a9faffb</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">“Starting with the August 2026 CU, SharePoint applies additional validation to the .NET types that can be used by BCS models</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be Starting with</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be Starting with"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_330d2cfd689a02d4" source="e_41e517acc2965ff0" target="e_56bee0a7d5aada83"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1d39c437bca92f1e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">“Starting with the August 2026 CU, SharePoint applies additional validation to the .NET types that can be used by BCS models</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be used by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be used by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_88e35542481b188e" source="e_6eac2ea8015cf2cc" target="e_f4957eaadf1d8c5f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are present in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_46352ff4102d5fc2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Types that are not present in this list are blocked to provide additional protection against potentially unsafe type usage.”</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are present in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are present in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_58905caf9da9a77f" source="e_6eac2ea8015cf2cc" target="e_71ed5a488ff96e7e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are blocked to provide additional protection against</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_92151ff5be43ee3e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Types that are not present in this list are blocked to provide additional protection against potentially unsafe type usage.”</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are blocked to provide additional protection against</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are blocked to provide additional protection against"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_a1ccc53fb913ac54" source="e_78b456fbfbf7a2f4" target="e_60992c6628dd7335"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">involve</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f5f9162bcda0e689</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Based on the excerpt above and the location of the code, we assessed that RCE would likely involve submitting a BDC (business data connectivity) model, or BDCM</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">involve</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["involve", "involves"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_abbb4792539a2660" source="e_83af7d9153bfe2b1" target="e_791de43fccfd7f2f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be imported within</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0067c05ecb1ad67c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">BDC is a service that allows external data sources (e.g., databases, web services, .NET assemblies, etc) to be imported and used within SharePoint as though they were SharePoint-native data sources</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be imported within</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be imported within"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_dcae69eb099140df" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_e6d6e7369c1cdeb1"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">know similar structure to CVE-2026-63520 from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_50da9ca794da5e7b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">CVE-2023-24955 in particular has a similar structure to CVE-2026-63520, which we know from implementing the 2023 flaw as part of a CVE-2023-29357 RCE chain</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">know similar structure to CVE-2026-63520 from</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">CVE</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["know similar structure to CVE-2026-63520 from"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_e33effbea49b274a" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_d098afd82f814fa4"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">know</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a8a47c3129275457</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">CVE-2023-24955 in particular has a similar structure to CVE-2026-63520, which we know from implementing the 2023 flaw as part of a CVE-2023-29357 RCE chain</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">know</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">CVE</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["know"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_3c2aab3a6730f1bf" source="e_d86bf1362e24a929" target="e_2d3885aa4dbbb2cf"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">patched</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e95393d28212f793</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When we examined the decompiled patched code, we found that the new validation function was being called in at least 16 locations, which gave us a reasonable roadmap for further investigation since they are all likely guarding interesting sinks</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">has patch</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["has patch", "patched"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_1f982bc1e0dc9d8f" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_9bbe75e9c910e585"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be looking at</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5a3e8ba9fceb97e7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Just looking at the function signature, we know this function is parsing a type from a LobSystem</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be looking at</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be looking at"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_87a7e9fa96ff2b8d" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_c8762019020c6b4f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be looking</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3feb6696a67b595d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Just looking at the function signature, we know this function is parsing a type from a LobSystem</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be looking</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be looking"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_74dbb8b00ee36832" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_ea78c12aa97286d0"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">make</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ca52d676f17dcf5d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">XML-based specs tend to be confusing, and we'd rather not make this entire blog post about the intricacies of the BDC spec</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">make</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["make", "makes"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_53bab1b2de5b45f6" source="e_3b1f2c268c6ccf12" target="e_2279292c015b9359"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">document</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4faa8e2efac5c991</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The official SharePoint GitHub docs actually document the BDCM schema in a parent-child hierarchy, which was helpful</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">document</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["document"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_4ecb2762fb9a085d" source="e_3b1f2c268c6ccf12" target="e_04e845d79fb1f65f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">document BDCM schema in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_126afa2f3d260f6a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The official SharePoint GitHub docs actually document the BDCM schema in a parent-child hierarchy, which was helpful</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">document BDCM schema in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["document BDCM schema in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_aac153c0c1ab048a" source="e_077bb703d76c8bd6" target="e_af26fda364ba9e72"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be needed to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_df3572547bbcd611</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This told us roughly how the layout needed to look, and more importantly, which attributes exist for each XML element</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be needed to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be needed to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_aabb2cadd1d9a63f" source="e_e163460c91338b08" target="e_a1dcdd289f57b065"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">told</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_94d6e13a734c3944</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This told us roughly how the layout needed to look, and more importantly, which attributes exist for each XML element</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">told</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["told"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_9e49b70dee63b128" source="e_273431069120d1d4" target="e_76780e7dcca5f8b4"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be hit</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_82f109704d55809d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">We eventually managed to get a valid BDCM model to hit Activator.CreateInstance and instantiate a System.Object, visible in the debugger (below)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be hit</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be hit"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_abf5a82715d4b792" source="e_5c980ac08d8e06db" target="e_9005adc286dd64cf"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">see</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6128135a2a7672ae</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As you can see above, System.Object was successfully passed to CreateInstance</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">see</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["see"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_8915bb610e8d51f0" source="e_e163460c91338b08" target="e_5523a40f730ea7d6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">resulted in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f77b7685fc6c8e09</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This resulted in this Start() overload being chosen over the static Start(String) overload that we wanted</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">result in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["result in", "resulted in", "results in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_2b454583320fda90" source="e_4881fab2f9c9099c" target="e_9005adc286dd64cf"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">code</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_76d7f3d75e9fa629</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This Instance-first method selection is shown in the decompiled DotNetAssembly/DotNetAssemblySystemUtility.cs code above, and from this we identified that for a useful gadget (i.e., a logical code object to use as an exploit primitive), we needed a Class that resolved a usable Instance type (or possibly a Class that had a useful Static type and no instance types, though we didn’t test this directly)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">code</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["code"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_fffc0fb78a452ddc" source="e_6cb7ff05f23b7da1" target="e_2f2483ca9ac5ab40"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be use as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_10f8cfc89ff5aea6</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This Instance-first method selection is shown in the decompiled DotNetAssembly/DotNetAssemblySystemUtility.cs code above, and from this we identified that for a useful gadget (i.e., a logical code object to use as an exploit primitive), we needed a Class that resolved a usable Instance type (or possibly a Class that had a useful Static type and no instance types, though we didn’t test this directly)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be use as</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be use as"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_fc3735621a3789d3" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_e3239ca4826a4553"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">needed</data><data key=