rse SSH tool for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d73c2d5fc6870b7e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S11</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/critical-vmware-vcenter-rce-flaw-exploited-for-reverse-ssh-access/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A recently patched critical vulnerability (CVE-2026-59310) in VMware vCenter Syslog Server is being exploited in an active campaign to deploy a reverse SSH tool for persistence and remote access</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be deploy reverse SSH tool for</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be deploy reverse SSH tool for"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_da474a97ccfd22e1" source="e_68a7b2b9d11ec625" target="e_fbd0f53534c11eb0"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be exploited by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_27375e1d26636100</data><data key="edge_source_id">S11</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/critical-vmware-vcenter-rce-flaw-exploited-for-reverse-ssh-access/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Broadcom disclosed CVE-2026-59310 on July 29 and described it as a critical directory traversal vulnerability in the vCenter Syslog server that could be exploited by an unauthenticated attacker with network access to execute arbitrary code</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be exploited by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be exploited by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_eaa405ec6fe74