6-55040-poc-exploit/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Microsoft has yet to confirm the bug has been exploited in the wild, even as it flags the flaw as a likely target</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">has been exploited in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["has been exploited in", "have been exploited in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_db4416a87784783f" source="e_8ea2d5e84baadda6" target="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">lead to unauthenticated remote code execution against vulnerable SharePoint server</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b7e21e945964ed4d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S18</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.helpnetsecurity.com/2026/08/13/microsoft-sharepoint-cve-2026-55040-poc-exploit/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When paired with another vulnerability, CVE-2026-63520, CVE-2026-55040 “could lead to unauthenticated remote code execution against a vulnerable SharePoint server”, according to NHS England Digital</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">lead to unauthenticated remote code execution against vulnerable SharePoint server</data><data key="edge_domain">CVE</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["lead to unauthenticated remote code execution against vulnerable SharePoint server"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_9f024c2e8cf58fcb" source="e_8ea2d5e84baadda6" target="e_fbfb70a00355d68e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">lead to unauthenticated remote code execution against vulnerable SharePoint server</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3b656f17a66af78f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S18</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.helpnetsecurity.com/2026/08/13/microsoft-sharepoint-cve-2026-55040-poc-exploit/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When paired with another vulnerability, CVE-2026-63520, CVE-2026-55040 “could lead to unauthenticated remote code execution against a vulnerable SharePoint server”, according to NHS England Digital</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">lead to unauthenticated remote code execution against vulnerable SharePoint server</data><data key="edge_domain">CVE</data><data key="edge_range">CVE</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["lead to unauthenticated remote code execution against vulnerable SharePoint server"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_24d5d68622228170" source="e_f815e0f3f0982d43" target="e_963d5ef03119d4bc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">Based on</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a295ac68306576a1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S19</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S19_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">BOD 26-04: Prioritizing Security Updates Based on Risk</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">Based on</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["Based on"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_2513883c57fcd98e" source="e_f815e0f3f0982d43" target="e_963d5ef03119d4bc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">Based on</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_cd9ce0efd830a131</data><data key="edge_source_id">S19</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S19_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This page contains a web-friendly version of the Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency’s Binding Operational Directive 26-04: Prioritizing Security Updates Based on Risk</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">Based on</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["Based on"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_3ff06d10dd775998" source="e_613f3f8d6df64501" target="e_de4bd852e64ddb08"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be operated by Department of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0e1bf7586b064b36</data><data key="edge_source_id">S19</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S19_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">These directives do not apply to statutorily defined “national security systems” or to certain systems operated by the Department of War or the Intelligence Community. 44 U.S.C. § 3553(b), (d), (e)(2), (e)(3)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be operated by Department of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be operated by Department of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_48da202aac3efe18" source="e_613f3f8d6df64501" target="e_def2164d8294bab8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be operated by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_957d1ec4e6c38087</data><data key="edge_source_id">S19</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S19_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">These directives do not apply to statutorily defined “national security systems” or to certain systems operated by the Department of War or the Intelligence Community. 44 U.S.C. § 3553(b), (d), (e)(2), (e)(3)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be operated by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be operated by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_72161d921ccdc53c" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_556b627b7c43e3ef"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">applies as Federal Civilian Executive Branch systems</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3d4baf7122966d15</data><data key="edge_source_id">S19</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S19_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This directive refers to the systems to which it applies as “Federal Civilian Executive Branch” systems, and to agencies operating those systems as “Federal Civilian Executive Branch” agencies</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">applies as Federal Civilian Executive Branch systems</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["applies as Federal Civilian Executive Branch systems"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_331f6fb0a08d6e46" source="e_20617c6c62d27119" target="e_3de2dcbc8f1d7a