s and outstanding issues in the implementation of this Directive</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be identifying cross-agency status in implementation of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be identifying cross-agency status in implementation of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_5c2fb519ff9a5149" source="e_5365cda3fbe79b23" target="e_3b8e724ba04c0cda"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be identifying outstanding issues in implementation of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d871db9439cf440e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S19</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S19_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">report to the Secretary of Homeland Security, the Director of OMB, and the National Cyber Director identifying cross-agency status and outstanding issues in the implementation of this Directive</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be identifying outstanding issues in implementation of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be identifying outstanding issues in implementation of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_58c41cde695f27c3" source="e_b8e5aea7bbbe87ad" target="e_96706e99cf570ef8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is important When</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_294a8d43e248e755</data><data key="edge_source_id">S19</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S19_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Technical impact depicts how much post-exploitation control an adversary gains over the affected asset and is similar to the Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) base score’s concept of “severity.” When evaluating technical impact, the definition of scope is particularly important</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is important When</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is important When"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_197476f9b5326eae" source="e_3a87cbc5f5034034" target="e_e6d2b84d9fd4abdb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">provides</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b15977e24e8b45c5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S19</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S19_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">1 Starred (*) are elements CISA provides to the CVE database through CISA’s Vulnrichment Program for every vulnerability with a CVE ID</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">provides</data><data key="edge_domain">Product</data><data key="edge_range">Product</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["provides", "provide"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_c9230557becba17c" source="e_ff6ebc9ca1f015bc" target="e_13304e9ecd6f65e9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">changes</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d331085804504173</data><data key="edge_source_id">S19</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S19_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, one valid mitigation is to remove the system from the internet; that action changes the value of “Publicly Exposed” from Yes to No and will shift the required timeline for further action, such as remediation, back</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">change</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["change", "changes"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_84ad902514b5b0f4" source="e_ff6ebc9ca1f015bc" target="e_effbc4fc49d0b75e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">shift required timeline for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8323514e88197467</data><data key="edge_source_id">S19</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S19_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, one valid mitigation is to remove the system from the internet; that action changes the value of “Publicly Exposed” from Yes to No and will shift the required timeline for further action, such as remediation, back</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">shift required timeline for</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["shift required timeline for"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_2faec0268b900f32" source="e_ff6ebc9ca1f015bc" target="e_edf56b768b8904e2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">shift required timeline such as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3bbd998953cbd3c5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S19</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S19_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, one valid mitigation is to remove the system from the internet; that action changes the value of “Publicly Exposed” from Yes to No and will shift the required timeline for further action, such as remediation, back</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">shift required timeline such as</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["shift required timeline such as"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_b479543f8074c163" source="e_ff6ebc9ca1f015bc" target="e_85ac34722b3aee08"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">shift</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_222ca7bc5636e48d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S19</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S19_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, one valid mitigation is to remove the system from the internet; that action changes the value of “Publicly Exposed” from Yes to No and will shift the required timeline for further action, such as remediation, back</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">shift</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["shift"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_ee2233560103a201" source="e_1bc3f1d1736a21b0" target="e_271803407533ce47"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">remain</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6bb1acca8cd837bf</data><data key="edge_source_id">S19</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.