 cryptographically generated addresses (CGAs), denial-of-service protection, and easier interoperability with non-Internet Protocol Security (IPsec)–capable peers</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is set of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is set of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_0627bf5906a3cfa8" source="e_8e81ce852cc92461" target="e_5a63fd7a393d6a05"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">added to IKE Protocol including authentication</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d89ed8f08de8284e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S45</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/cisa-critical-windows-ike-extension-flaw-now-exploited-in-attacks/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Also known as MS-IKEE, this is a set of additional capabilities Microsoft added to the IKE Protocol, including authentication via cryptographically generated addresses (CGAs), denial-of-service protection, and easier interoperability with non-Internet Protocol Security (IPsec)–capable peers</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">added to IKE Protocol including authentication</data><data key="edge_domain">Vendor</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["added to IKE Protocol including authentication"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_9af3b8c06632404e" source="e_8e81ce852cc92461" target="e_5a63fd7a393d6a05"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">added via generated addresses</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_36a2a69f460fba4d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S45</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/cisa-critical-windows-ike-extension-flaw-now-exploited-in-attacks/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Also known as MS-IKEE, this is a set of additional capabilities Microsoft added to the IKE Protocol, including authentication via cryptographically generated addresses (CGAs), denial-of-service protection, and easier interoperability with non-Internet Protocol Security (IPsec)–capable peers</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">added via generated addresses</data><data key="edge_domain">Vendor</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["added via generated addresses"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_2740ab97f7975aad" source="e_8e81ce852cc92461" target="e_5a63fd7a393d6a05"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">added via easier interoperability with non-Internet Protocol Security</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_cd2f045a47635b4e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S45</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/cisa-critical-windows-ike-extension-flaw-now-exploited-in-attacks/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Also known as MS-IKEE, this is a set of additional capabilities Microsoft added to the IKE Protocol, including authentication via cryptographically generated addresses (CGAs), denial-of-service protection, and easier interoperability with non-Internet Protocol Security (IPsec)–capable peers</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">added via easier interoperability with non-Internet Protocol Security</data><data key="edge_domain">Vendor</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["added via easier interoperability with non-Internet Protocol Security"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_5f1cfe0047f68ce8" source="e_698ece6b18d3f69a" target="e_e89a40e488525a7c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be Tracked as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_07790ffd05ee8ffc</data><data key="edge_source_id">S45</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/cisa-critical-windows-ike-extension-flaw-now-exploited-in-attacks/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Tracked as CVE-2026-33824, this RCE vulnerability impacts all supported Windows 10, Windows 11, and Windows Server releases, and it allows attackers without privileges to gain code execution by sending maliciously crafted packets to unpatched Windows systems through UDP ports 500 or 4500</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be Tracked as</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">CVE</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be Tracked as"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_19c9cfeece7fb264" source="e_d11166eda6870fd7" target="e_c06c4370e6687188"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be issued during April 2026 Patch</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5dfb0df42a0ef163</data><data key="edge_source_id">S45</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/cisa-critical-windows-ike-extension-flaw-now-exploited-in-attacks/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">"Double free in Windows IKE Extension allows an unauthorized attacker to execute code over a network," Microsoft says in an advisory issued during the April 2026 Patch Tuesday when it addressed the vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be issued during April 2026 Patch</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be issued during April 2026 Patch"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_982e31ba8cd93be9" source="e_d11166eda6870fd7" target="e_980e49a4f0d05bbe"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be issued during</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_564e718086b5d7c7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S45</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/cisa-critical-windows-ike-extension-flaw-now-exploited-in-attacks/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">"Double free in Windows IKE Extension allows an unauthorized attacker to execute code over a network," Microsoft says in an advisory issued during the April 2026 Patch Tuesday when it addressed the vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be issued during</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be issued during"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_3b67e4c51e8e7027" source="e_b82be424e7d21f94" target="e_a7523256c9515f68"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">enable</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_fe600c019389ed1c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S45</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/cisa-critical-windows-ike-extension-flaw-now-exploited-in-attacks/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">"An unauthenticated attacker could send specially crafted packets to a Windows machine with Internet Key Exchange (IKE) version 2 enabled, which could enable remote code execution."</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><d