ertion_id">a_288f6877bf38c58a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S45</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/cisa-critical-windows-ike-extension-flaw-now-exploited-in-attacks/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Although Microsoft has yet to update its advisory to flag it as exploited, CISA has added the flaw to its catalog of actively exploited vulnerabilities and ordered U.S</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">has catalog of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["has catalog of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_01300afc5b9018d6" source="e_3e66ae108275dff7" target="e_bb4b95215298a6c6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">have begun</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c53b8932a1cee74b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S45</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/cisa-critical-windows-ike-extension-flaw-now-exploited-in-attacks/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Last week, it also warned that ransomware operations have begun using a Microsoft SharePoint RCE vulnerability in attacks after confirming in-the-wild exploitation in early July</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">reported</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">have begun</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Product</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["have begun"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_f4f54d25163bc887" source="e_8e81ce852cc92461" target="e_716714868d3df08f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">disclosed</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_289688d1616cb5cc</data><data key="edge_source_id">S46</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.sentrium.co.uk/labs/windows-ike-service-extensions-vulnerability-enables-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In April 2026, Microsoft disclosed and patched a critical remote code execution vulnerability affecting the Windows Internet Key Exchange Service Extensions</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">disclosed</data><data key="edge_domain">Vendor</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["disclosed"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_dcabb714735c2df9" source="e_c7a7735bf61b8084" target="e_e89a40e488525a7c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be Tracked as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6e2d5028d7ec38ca</data><data key="edge_source_id">S46</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.sentrium.co.uk/labs/windows-ike-service-extensions-vulnerability-enables-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Tracked as CVE-2026-33824, the issue was addressed as part of Microsoft’s April 2026 Patch Tuesday release</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be Tracked as</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">CVE</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be Tracked as"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_a8de3486abfba4e2" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_3d33bcab7851ab3b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is exposed to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_94aedfe34fce604e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S46</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.sentrium.co.uk/labs/windows-ike-service-extensions-vulnerability-enables-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As a result, it is frequently exposed to untrusted networks and processes unauthenticated traffic as part of normal operation</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is exposed to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is exposed to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_8a121308d39bb3be" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_93a987c6ae52ebdd"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is exposed to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_422147349b401c68</data><data key="edge_source_id">S46</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.sentrium.co.uk/labs/windows-ike-service-extensions-vulnerability-enables-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As a result, it is frequently exposed to untrusted networks and processes unauthenticated traffic as part of normal operation</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is exposed to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is exposed to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_c19743eaf8bedf4e" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_f6693345b0c05574"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">arises from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_cb254eb8276666f8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S46</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.sentrium.co.uk/labs/windows-ike-service-extensions-vulnerability-enables-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Specifically, the vulnerability arises from a double free condition, where the same region of memory is released more than once during the processing of specially crafted IKE packets</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">arises from</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["arises from"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_6f646ac5c9f03aef" source="e_b89cef742f5e5473" target="e_f6693345b0c05574"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is released more than once</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_71c167dcbcb80367</data><data key="edge_source_id">S46</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.sentrium.co.uk/labs/windows-ike-service-extensions-vulnerability-enables-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Specifically, the vulnerability arises from a double free condition, where the same region of memory is released more than once during the processing of specially crafted IKE packets</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is released more than once</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is released more than once"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_1dd5d64cb149305c" source="e_b89cef742f5e5473" target="e_f6693345b0c05574"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is released during processing of crafted IKE packets</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4bf481c4a98462a6</data><data key="edge_source_id">S46</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.sentrium.co.uk/labs/windows-ike-service-extensions-vulnerability-enables-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Specifically, the vulnerability arises from a double free condition, where the same region of memory is released more than once during the processing of specially crafted IKE packets</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is released during processing of crafted IKE packets</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is released during processing of crafted IKE packets"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_c218f20c007f7002" source="e_b89cef742f5e5473" target="e_f6693345b0c05574"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is released</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_80b4113d422fb912</data><data key="edge_source_id">S46</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.sentrium.co.uk/labs/windows-ike-service-extensions-vulnerability-enables-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Specifically, the vulnerability arises from a double free condition, where the same region of memory is released more than once during the processing of specially crafted IKE packets</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">has released</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["has released", "is released", "released"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_da56fe8cd9cbce3e" source="e_d7e463de17faf1c1" target="e_40277cc0f3735575"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be allowing</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_03fab61f0ae39c9d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S46</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.sentrium.co.uk/labs/windows-ike-service-extensions-vulnerability-enables-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This class of vulnerability can lead to heap corruption, potentially allowing an attacker to influence memory allocation behaviour and ultimately control execution flow</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be allowing</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be allowing"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_4f4f05ad40fc4946" source="e_d7e463de17faf1c1" target="e_d77f522e6a8e6b56"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be allowing</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_fe31d1bd0a3ad615</data><data key="edge_source_id">S46</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.sentrium.co.uk/labs/windows-ike-service-extensions-vulnerability-enables-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This class of vulnerability can lead to heap corruption, potentially allowing an attacker to influence memory allocation behaviour and ultimately control execution flow</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be allowing</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be allowing"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_a129dc1ae752550f" source="e_d7e463de17faf1c1" target="e_c2923e925aa6f233"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be allowing</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4bc37a1a5197b094</data><data key="edge_source_id">S46</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.sentrium.co.uk/labs/windows-ike-service-extensions-vulnerability-enables-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This class of vulnerability can lead to heap corruption, potentially allowing an attacker to influence memory allocation behaviour and ultimately control execution flow</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be allowing</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be allowing"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_243b34265fceea7c" source="e_d7e463de17faf1c1" target="e_6598fc48ab305673"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">lead to heap corruption</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e813190ab240a8ce</data><data key="edge_source_id">S46</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.sentrium.co.uk/labs/windows-ike-service-extensions-vulnerability-enables-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This class of vulnerability can lead to heap corruption, potentially allowing an attacker to influence memory allocation behaviour and ultimately control execution flow</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">lead to heap corruption</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["lead to heap corruption"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_695f4829c86b611c" source="e_d7e463de17faf1c1" target="e_ac626a21264496c0"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">lead to heap corruption</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_43be0d8eec4fea4e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S46</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.sentrium.co.uk/labs/windows-ike-service-extensions-vulnerability-enables-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This class of vulnerability can lead to heap corruption, potentially allowing an attacker to influence memory allocation behaviour and ultimately control execution flow</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">lead to heap corruption</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["lead to heap corruption"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_938eab38eed59637" source="e_d7e463de17faf1c1" target="e_954b7bdeb70d2263"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">lead to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_98dca085622fd081</data><data key="edge_source_id">S46</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.sentrium.co.uk/labs/windows-ike-service-extensions-vulnerability-enables-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This class of vulnerability can lead to heap corruption, potentially allowing an attacker to influence memory allocation behaviour and ultimately control execution flow</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">lead to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["lead to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_cc9781fa89269350" source="e_e163460c91338b08" target="e_a7cb80b36d59b0ed"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">introduces</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_220341de551bdd10</data><data key="edge_source_id">S46</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.sentrium.co.uk/labs/windows-ike-service-extensions-vulnerability-enables-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In practical terms, this introduces a pathway to remote code execution within the context of the IKE service</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">introduces</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["introduces"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_d0a6a590c3568c9f" source="e_d8d9b706557f592e" target="e_7ee1ff4a70457dd7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be send crafted IKE traffic to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_91fa535ec1dcc37e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S46</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.sentrium.co.uk/labs/windows-ike-service-extensions-vulnerability-enables-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">An attacker only requires the ability to send specially crafted IKE traffic to a vulnerable system</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be send crafted IKE traffic to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be send crafted IKE traffic to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_27773fa96e863244" source="e_bb46d8ce39883e67" target="e_9d9c39e91777bd72"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is reachable via</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_69329b3b5d75531a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S46</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.sentrium.co.uk/labs/windows-ike-service-extensions-vulnerability-enables-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The affected code path is reachable via UDP ports 500 and 4500, which are the standard ports used by IKE and IKE NAT traversal</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is reachable via</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is reachable via"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_7708f9499c760617" source="e_2814255e6d9edcc5" target="e_9ffb7cbec78fa95f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8b1e6d3c32ab6da7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S46</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.sentrium.co.uk/labs/windows-ike-service-extensions-vulnerability-enables-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The affected code path is reachable via UDP ports 500 and 4500, which are the standard ports used by IKE and IKE NAT traversal</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be used by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be used by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_4f1402faf36d90d6" source="e_2814255e6d9edcc5" target="e_b77ad8d489ccdc25"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3848bcae31de3595</data><data key="edge_source_id">S46</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.sentrium.co.uk/labs/windows-ike-service-extensions-vulnerability-enables-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The affected code path is reachable via UDP ports 500 and 4500, which are the standard ports used by IKE and IKE NAT traversal</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be used by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be used by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_d464fee803c25133" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_c3b059ee268b1ded"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">affects wide range of supported Windows platforms including Windows Server 2016 through to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_47c886c29e319b15</data><data key="edge_source_id">S46</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.sentrium.co.uk/labs/windows-ike-service-extensions-vulnerability-enables-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The vulnerability affects a wide range of supported Windows platforms, including Windows Server 2016 through to Windows Server 2025, as well as multiple versions of Windows 10 and Windows 11 across different system architectures</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">affects wide range of supported Windows platforms including Windows Server 2016 through to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Product</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["affects wide range of supported Windows platforms including Windows Server 2016 through to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_67000785a4ff7ab2" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_5f5c688adc26f126"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">affects wide range of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_53f1f3512a99b053</data><data key="edge_source_id">S46</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.sentrium.co.uk/labs/windows-ike-service-extensions-vulnerability-enables-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The vulnerability affects a wide range of supported Windows platforms, including Windows Server 2016 through to Windows Server 2025, as well as multiple versions of Windows 10 and Windows 11 across different system architectures</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">affects wide range of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["affects wide range of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_52f83d4aeb556860" source="e_556b627b7c43e3ef" target="e_dc2cefbd5c093801"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be considered</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4ead5716bc9da5e7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S46</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.sentrium.co.uk/labs/windows-ike-service-extensions-vulnerability-enables-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Systems that have not applied the April 2026 security updates should be considered vulnerable</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be considered</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be considered"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_fb1450d401cfb626" source="e_16ea76003b3fd67e" target="e_26aa4de4630a84d2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">result in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b5bcae8fdd579976</data><data key="edge_source_id">S46</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.sentrium.co.uk/labs/windows-ike-service-extensions-vulnerability-enables-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Successful exploitation would result in remote code execution within the context of the IKE service</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">result in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["result in", "resulted in", "results in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_ca894b0b34e19950" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_5c5d3d12f56bd772"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">gain complete control of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_bf5c848d32ebdde6</data><data key="edge_source_id">S46</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.sentrium.co.uk/labs/windows-ike-service-extensions-vulnerability-enables-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">An attacker could gain complete control of the affected system, deploy additional tooling, and potentially move laterally into other parts of the environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">gain complete control of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["gain complete control of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_a3afac45f9fae1e8" source="e_9ed9f9c2275e8e7e" target="e_e8b392d409ccf57d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is significant for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a46fc2e14cc88525</data><data key="edge_source_id">S46</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.sentrium.co.uk/labs/windows-ike-service-extensions-vulnerability-enables-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The impact is particularly significant for organisations operating VPN gateways or Always On VPN deployments</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is significant for</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is significant for"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_c8b37cc1fa84cb16" source="e_61253fa74e0643d5" target="e_1569a84bf6953ca8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">provide direct access into</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_be6e01c60a28ef54</data><data key="edge_source_id">S46</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.sentrium.co.uk/labs/windows-ike-service-extensions-vulnerability-enables-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A compromise at this layer can undermine network segmentation and provide direct access into internal infrastructure</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">provide direct access into</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["provide direct access into"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_df2d568aa3d58a8d" source="e_8e81ce852cc92461" target="e_e89a40e488525a7c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">released security updates for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ebcaa778a3fc0f06</data><data key="edge_source_id">S46</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.sentrium.co.uk/labs/windows-ike-service-extensions-vulnerability-enables-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Microsoft released security updates for CVE-2026-33824 on 14 April 2026</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">released security updates for</data><data key="edge_domain">Vendor</data><data key="edge_range">CVE</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["released security updates for"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_63516d752559bf8f" source="e_5299db4a3b7653a2" target="e_3d33bcab7851ab3b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">expose IKE services to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_40d96594136d1427</data><data key="edge_source_id">S46</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.sentrium.co.uk/labs/windows-ike-service-extensions-vulnerability-enables-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Organisations should prioritise patching systems that expose IKE services to untrusted networks</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">expose IKE services to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["expose IKE services to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_22b1bf128ed196d8" source="e_d7ab1020fcb494c5" target="e_6a5b18796f0b7110"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be applied</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_deb78b55b2cac158</data><data key="edge_source_id">S46</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.sentrium.co.uk/labs/windows-ike-service-extensions-vulnerability-enables-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-33824</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Where patching cannot be applied immediately, exposure should be reduced wherever possible</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edg