source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_ca335c133f4134dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are constant over</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_452006838f548f11</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">the intrinsic characteristics of a vulnerability that are constant over time and across user environments</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are constant over</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are constant over"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_3e1283595cdc2af1" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_ca335c133f4134dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are across user environments over</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_faac0f485cc9b000</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">the intrinsic characteristics of a vulnerability that are constant over time and across user environments</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are across user environments over</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are across user environments over"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_55a0a47d7e9c9ec6" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_3d75e6dbcbfb5033"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are across</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6f454d032b93a3d3</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">the intrinsic characteristics of a vulnerability that are constant over time and across user environments</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are across</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are across"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_4fb821a6f7c7a7d9" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_7ee1ff4a70457dd7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">refer thing to formally as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_065b58dac1c7ca3b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">That is, they represent characteristics of the “thing that is vulnerable”, which we refer to formally as the “vulnerable system”</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">refer thing to formally as</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["refer thing to formally as"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_43b790491aa83e09" source="e_546996a8b2a435a8" target="e_e4537cb8e78c8b83"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">includes</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ca84448d562063e8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">While the vulnerable system is typically a software application, operating system, module, driver, etc. (or possibly a hardware device), the subsequent system could be any of those examples but also includes human safety</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">include</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["include", "includes"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_d22da7b2ed280ddd" source="e_838a95b0b63fa880" target="e_ca335c133f4134dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">change over</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_32c6e65d031eba6d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Threat metric group reflects the characteristics of a vulnerability related to threat that may change over time but not necessarily across user environments</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">change over</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["change over", "changes over", "do change over"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_5f9d04d641b90767" source="e_abe69e34c599411a" target="e_ca335c133f4134dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">change over</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_72e1a5c4efa81ddf</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The values found in this metric group may change over time</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">change over</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["change over", "changes over", "do change over"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_46cbed2e136bb674" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_c8dcccc9a9dca201"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are relevant to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f379fc3a766047d7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Environmental metric group represents the characteristics of a vulnerability that are relevant and unique to a particular consumers’ environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are relevant to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are relevant to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_2179565c50186d27" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_c8dcccc9a9dca201"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are unique to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_35ab713e2ef6167f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Environmental metric group represents the characteristics of a vulnerability that are relevant and unique to a particular consumers’ environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are unique to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are unique to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_f607b3041f27c257" source="e_1e8ea1b42ca055ae" target="e_ecedfcb33ae54209"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">include</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2980cda20963ef44</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Considerations include the presence of security controls which may mitigate some or all consequences of a successful attack, and the relative importance of a vulnerable system within a technology infrastructure</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">include</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["include", "includes"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_d42f67fcf2d68acb" source="e_371e2a8932c3cb22" target="e_768bf52735c34131"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">includes</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_03b35db034b6e3d0</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Supplemental metric group includes metrics that provide context as well as describe and measure additional extrinsic attributes of a vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">include</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["include", "includes"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_f2f1aacdba4ee8d8" source="e_768bf52735c34131" target="e_466e6