e_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Supplemental metric group includes metrics that provide context as well as describe and measure additional extrinsic attributes of a vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">measure additional extrinsic attributes of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["measure additional extrinsic attributes of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_3f57efd65e57341b" source="e_12024175e2291ad7" target="e_768bf52735c34131"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be apply significant severity to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_32f5b27869e5f4a1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The response to each metric within the Supplemental metric group is to be determined by the CVSS consumer, allowing the usage of an end-user risk analysis system to apply locally significant severity to the metrics and values</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be apply significant severity to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be apply significant severity to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_60382de961a3ba68" source="e_12024175e2291ad7" target="e_a9ed604eb1323e31"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be apply significant severity to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5dc558895a55145f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The response to each metric within the Supplemental metric group is to be determined by the CVSS consumer, allowing the usage of an end-user risk analysis system to apply locally significant severity to the metrics and values</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be apply significant severity to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be apply significant severity to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_a521f0c773051391" source="e_80b852b98e6b518c" target="e_cd0a45b2a1788da0"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be useful when</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b763a44b0571ff5f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The User Guide contains scoring rubrics for the Base Metrics that may be useful when scoring</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be useful when</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be useful when"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_726e9f1f1cb158ca" source="e_80b852b98e6b518c" target="e_f6498126c94c6f96"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are assigned values by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_51f2fa0877ad2519</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When the Base metrics are assigned values by an analyst, the Base metrics assessment results in a score ranging from 0.0 to 10.0</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are assigned values by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are assigned values by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_57d15cff1ba1e894" source="e_d15e9e1afe2a9d2f" target="e_491a87f4c4b335f8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be posed by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d4552025a03d2301</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Base metrics assessment can then be further refined by assessing the Threat and Environmental metrics in order to more accurately reflect the relative severity posed by a vulnerability to a user’s environment at a specific point in time</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be posed by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be posed by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_8a1e7520a96e377d" source="e_290d8da624d84fb0" target="e_a0ef75f1f1ee68c4"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">possess</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_743fe19665302c94</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Generally, the Base metrics are specified by vulnerability bulletin analysts, product vendors, or application vendors because they typically possess the most accurate information about the characteristics of a vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">possess</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["possess"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_4019db096ff5e240" source="e_45b3e78147f50a23" target="e_ea4e8774919b4516"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used to derive</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8ab184504e894ea2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Assessing CVSS metrics also produces a vector string, a textual representation of the metric values used to derive a quantitative score and qualitative rating for the vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be used to derive</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be used to derive"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_9048eb7a4b288d8e" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has perfect knowledge of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_43bad9961b38fabb</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Note that all metrics should be assessed under the assumption that the attacker has perfect knowledge of the vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">has perfect knowledge of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["has perfect knowledge of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_935e5ff68154f315" source="e_768bf52735c34131" target="e_f8b520c0a0b6460f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used to calculate</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_341f07e3f45f1d16</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Numerical CVSS Scores have very different meanings based on the metrics used to calculate them</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be used to calculate</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be used to calculate"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_bae80e9c1a3baee3" source="e_b189ba3fb7ef7706" target="e_1af6c78accf2e433"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be labeled</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7abe7d1a7ca90cb9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Therefore, numerical CVSS scores should be labeled using nomenclature that communicates the metrics used in its generation</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be labeled</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be labeled"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_f2d4b794a77834ae" source="e_768bf52735c34131" target="e_bbcb8ea999353380"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f453ecc2d64b2b48</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Therefore, numerical CVSS scores should be labeled using nomenclature that communicates the metrics used in its generation</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be used in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be used in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_2717ea0337667154" source="e_9e3f8e0349f649b1" target="e_d800caf744b5709e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is responsibility of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e44ec34543a72f51</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The application of Environmental and Threat metrics is the responsibility of the CVSS consumer</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is responsibility of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is responsibility of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_d3c78c5bae4d9002" source="e_845db19a5f318ea7" target="e_d800caf744b5709e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is responsibility of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6e7d4d62f793ae32</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The application of Environmental and Threat metrics is the responsibility of the CVSS consumer</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is responsibility of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is responsibility of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_3a22d92b757eadb7" source="e_0aeb5fdf6effbdc8" target="e_51321b750147cbd0"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be enumerated as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_282c4f68ac056184</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Assessment providers such as product maintainers and other public/private entities such as the National Vulnerability Database (NVD) typically provide only the Base Scores enumerated as CVSS-B</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be enumerated as</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be enumerated as"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_60e6850a6e101d04" source="e_ba6a59ae6b0db851" target="e_5e3014756335417a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">result in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0fc74000ea7ae8fc</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The absence of explicit Threat and/or Environmental metric selections will still result in a complete score using default (“Not Defined”) values</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">result in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["result in", "resulted in", "results in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_7b97a9eb6218cb80" source="e_0b1f826002e28a94" target="e_5e3014756335417a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">result in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4fc1f9170278144d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The absence of explicit Threat and/or Environmental metric selections will still result in a complete score using default (“Not Defined”) values</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">result in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["result in", "resulted in", "results in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_f0b2a90a3748eeef" source="e_c00a4051d0530e03" target="e_7105a374c44c5518"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">reflect characteristics of thing As</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d539788c49e910ed</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As previously mentioned, the Exploitability metrics reflect the characteristics of the “thing that is vulnerable”, which we refer to formally as the vulnerable system</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">reflect characteristics of thing As</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["reflect characteristics of thing As"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_f0d868b429f31aba" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_7ee1ff4a70457dd7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">refer thing to formally as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_bf46cd7996c6b2b7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As previously mentioned, the Exploitability metrics reflect the characteristics of the “thing that is vulnerable”, which we refer to formally as the vulnerable system</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">refer thing to formally as</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["refer thing to formally as"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_c6453e4c5a5c6c9b" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_2676df0405400172"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">lead to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_47a452a2deb43c50</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Therefore, each of the Exploitability metrics listed below should be assessed relative to the vulnerable system, and reflect the properties of the vulnerability that lead to a successful attack</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">lead to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["lead to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_77977bafbcd78085" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_277f0117c004b170"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has advanced knowledge of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f2bf619a5f5996b4</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When assessing Base metrics, it should be assumed that the attacker has advanced knowledge of the target system, including general configuration and default defense mechanisms (e.g., built-in firewalls, rate limits, traffic policing)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">has advanced knowledge of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["has advanced knowledge of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_6dee226c23268977" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_b8ee2c28df4dc72b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">results in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_799cf20d2e1b094d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, exploiting a vulnerability that results in repeatable, deterministic success should still be considered a Low value for Attack Complexity, independent of the attacker's knowledge or capabilities</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">result in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["result in", "resulted in", "results in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_36a9f8493d1c18a8" source="e_d76f0b71c9538da5" target="e_fcae9732e4e96feb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be considered</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5a8d928865aaa114</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, exploiting a vulnerability that results in repeatable, deterministic success should still be considered a Low value for Attack Complexity, independent of the attacker's knowledge or capabilities</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be considered</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be considered"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_32c861909192e522" source="e_d76f0b71c9538da5" target="e_454f93ad983bcfc4"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be considered</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0de5c44f045ae568</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, exploiting a vulnerability that results in repeatable, deterministic success should still be considered a Low value for Attack Complexity, independent of the attacker's knowledge or capabilities</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be considered</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be considered"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_a8209bf9d7fdf013" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_571bc10d653316b8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be exploited from across</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b85fcf0b271bcef5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The assumption is that the number of potential attackers for a vulnerability that could be exploited from across a network is larger than the number of potential attackers that could exploit a vulnerability requiring physical access to a device, and therefore warrants a greater severity</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be exploited from across</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be exploited from across"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_fb28401171dd0881" source="e_6c929bb8a42a9b8c" target="e_b4e364ab91d013d5"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is larger than number of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ca641f74ab50df45</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The assumption is that the number of potential attackers for a vulnerability that could be exploited from across a network is larger than the number of potential attackers that could exploit a vulnerability requiring physical access to a device, and therefore warrants a grea