a><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["emerge as consequence of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_68b7630d509ebb28" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_92078ff0ec595868"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">does take action to overcome</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3ad69f1515a78ee8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">If the attacker does not take action to overcome these conditions, the attack may succeed only occasionally or not succeed at all</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">does take action to overcome</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["does take action to overcome"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_3a4252d4c7ee8c4c" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_92078ff0ec595868"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be overcome</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_fe0102359965e2ef</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">If the attacker does not take action to overcome these conditions, the attack may succeed only occasionally or not succeed at all</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be overcome</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be overcome"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_05bcb0ba75c68534" source="e_4676679afd99eed0" target="e_1b50c049dec6c218"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">describes level of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_70656c2765ff104f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This metric describes the level of privileges an attacker must possess prior to successfully exploiting the vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">describes level of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["describes level of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_a6cf0df0cbf179e3" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_1b50c049dec6c218"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">possess to exploiting vulnerability</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4e375b3124446bf1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This metric describes the level of privileges an attacker must possess prior to successfully exploiting the vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">possess to exploiting vulnerability</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["possess to exploiting vulnerability"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_9756f07056e04d49" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_1b50c049dec6c218"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">possess</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_dc2b0340bc070024</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This metric describes the level of privileges an attacker must possess prior to successfully exploiting the vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">possess</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["possess"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_6370918740047063" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_4916cc2d145603f5"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">obtains privileged credentials prior to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_acc957da15e999c6</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The method by which the attacker obtains privileged credentials prior to the attack (e.g., free trial accounts), is outside the scope of this metric</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">obtains privileged credentials prior to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["obtains privileged credentials prior to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_cb2a4b2583a0149b" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_333716f10a881b90"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">obtains privileged credentials</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_80e4f4bf348234f7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The method by which the attacker obtains privileged credentials prior to the attack (e.g., free trial accounts), is outside the scope of this metric</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">obtains privileged credentials</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["obtains privileged credentials"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_1736ba87a820bd6d" source="e_028c7b1d0f837f74" target="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is other than</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_326d0c90ce3377e5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This metric captures the requirement for a human user, other than the attacker, to participate in the successful compromise of the vulnerable system</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is other than</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is other than"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_f31531a2afa332cd" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be exploited at will of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9b3f2b2aed971117</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This metric determines whether the vulnerability can be exploited solely at the will of the attacker, or whether a separate user (or user-initiated process) must participate in some manner</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be exploited at will of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be exploited at will of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_1aafe917be55fdfa" source="e_dda76eeedb5c35a4" target="e_7ee1ff4a70457dd7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">subvert protections built into</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7d3ecda8d7fff677</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">These interactions would be considered involuntary and do not require that the user actively subvert protections built into the vulnerable system</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">subvert protections built into</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["subvert protections built into"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_a0ffdd565d185b50" source="e_e8580183c3bd0734" target="e_7ee1ff4a70457dd7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be built into</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8b06747b8402f024</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">These interactions would be considered involuntary and do not require that the user actively subvert protections built into the vulnerable system</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be built into</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be built into"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_f40dc3ac1f742263" source="e_b3c77c913f52e355" target="e_8913949ce3c45f5f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be considered</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_09b8d25e4ae09132</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">These interactions would be considered involuntary and do not require that the user actively subvert protections built into the vulnerable system</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be considered</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be considered"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_2dffeff60da1eb76" source="e_75ac4e09b3f2b875" target="e_2228b2b192c550b5"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">capture effects of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5234fbfe557d0670</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Impact metrics capture the effects of a successfully exploited vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">capture effects of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["capture effects of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_af2d71e9e1edcf1d" source="e_d4cff6070f136c90" target="e_35b2194131dcbc9a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">constrain impacts to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_29f9ca91cf639eb9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Analysts should constrain impacts to a reasonable, final outcome which they are confident an attacker is able to achieve</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">constrain impacts to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["constrain impacts to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_967e765da715c3c1" source="e_d4cff6070f136c90" target="e_57598c70746601d2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">constrain</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_de903422b86abe07</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Analysts should constrain impacts to a reasonable, final outcome which they are confident an attacker is able to achieve</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">constrain</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["constrain"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_fe07129fef4041dc" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_f3d00477181497a6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">requires read-only permissions prior to being</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_bffdf8359dd3e0a4</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, consider a vulnerability that requires read-only permissions prior to being able to exploit the vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">requires read-only permissions prior to being</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["requires read-only permissions prior to being"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_e83ba32df3c34e2d" source="e_5abf948c6bee4fdf" target="e_f3d00477181497a6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be able</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_35ec01c6bb957b7e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, consider a vulnerability that requires read-only permissions prior to being able to exploit the vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be able</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be able"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_53bdf4fcc9388a79" source="e_8f5263a93ee3ad05" target="e_f2dca16215b933e8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">write</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f99b5a4cb2770464</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">After successful exploitation, the attacker maintains the same level of read access, and gains write access</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">write</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["write"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_e09c5e6c7e959c23" source="e_29bb0e9d5a84c984" target="e_f2dca16215b933e8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">write</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a30153ba8e9b111f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">After successful exploitation, the attacker maintains the same level of read access, and gains write access</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">write</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["write"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_37e547fc1030b01f" source="e_b06e479590c522c6" target="e_d7268769fbad72a0"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">reference</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_96ce31569721947e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, if an attacker starts with partial access to restricted information (Confidentiality Low) and successful exploitation of the vulnerability results in complete loss in confidentiality (Confidentiality High), then the resultant CVSS Base metric value should reference the “end game” Impact metric value (Confidentiality High)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">references</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["references", "reference"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_301322a7624bce5d" source="e_61d75bfb2ba29a45" target="e_856f644b1eea7665"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">use conceptual model of system of interest When establishing boundaries for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b77f11f00e7e8617</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When establishing the boundaries for the Vulnerable System metric values, assessment providers should use the conceptual model of a system of interest</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">use conceptual model of system of interest When establishing boundaries for</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["use conceptual model of system of interest When establishing boundaries for"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_5f38828284a43f93" source="e_61d75bfb2ba29a45" target="e_f52f19c613910d1c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">use</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ed8f08fc7d531b29</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When establishing the boundaries for the Vulnerable System metric values, assessment providers should use the conceptual model of a system of interest</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">use</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["use", "uses", "do use", "Uses"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_e4a65fd3d1f17f9e" source="e_c6a340213fcac165" target="e_f2cdc47ec4f51081"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is defined as set of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_821f501350e8e31a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Formally, a system of interest for scoring a vulnerability is defined as the set of computing logic that executes in an environment with a coherent function and set of security policies</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is defined as set of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is defined as set of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_212315f811b8808b" source="e_3521c6ce31419359" target="e_c6c46476c8ff74de"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">executes in environment with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b53a6845f3cb7200</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Formally, a system of interest for scoring a vulnerability is defined as the set of computing logic that executes in an environment with a coherent function and set of security policies</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">executes in environment with</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["executes in environment with"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_a9b63d271e7ebcb5" source="e_3521c6ce31419359" target="e_33b897287e267e17"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">executes in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3ab1bdc882ec9d8a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Formally, a system of interest for scoring a vulnerability is defined as the set of computing logic that executes in an environment with a coherent function and set of security policies</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">executes in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["executes in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_5520868f001ea775" source="e_76352b9065576337" target="e_de24cb3f3fac6c9e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">serves purpose from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_45119f1a4e2a14ad</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A technology product or a solution that serves a purpose or function from a consumer's perspective is considered a system (e.g., a server, workstation, containerized service, etc.)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">serves purpose from</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["serves purpose from"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_f037fa5111325697" source="e_76352b9065576337" target="e_2dcafecf60ea08b2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">serves</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2b3b5b257b0291f0</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A technology product or a solution that serves a purpose or function from a consumer's perspective is considered a system (e.g., a server, workstation, containerized service, etc.)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">serves</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["serves"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_0b16344afbe21bea" source="e_93d8650fe6b85a54" target="e_c9f7ebbebae4fbbf"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">provides</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_053c904c74aac860</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When a system provides its functionality solely to another system, or it is designed to be exclusively used by another system, then together they are considered as the system of interest for scoring</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">provides</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["provides", "provide"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_2deb61d31fbfdc53" source="e_57e6975d8ca79e1f" target="e_008c5289d9ee1bc8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4ff80ab0716e4f3c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, a database used solely by a smart speaker is considered a part of that smart speaker system</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be used by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be used by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_2108fa195c12657c" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_008c5289d9ee1bc8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">serves</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ab14837f5dfce904</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Both the database and the smart speaker it serves would be considered the vulnerable system if a vulnerability in that database leads to the malfunction of the smart speaker</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">serves</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["serves"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_788e14a23ddcbd7a" source="e_57e6975d8ca79e1f" target="e_7ee1ff4a70457dd7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be considered</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_29d612610a6bc53f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Both the database and the smart speaker it serves would be considered the vulnerable system if a vulnerability in that database leads to the malfunction of the smart speaker</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be considered</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be considered"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_3ceb351d2ecc5953" source="e_008c5289d9ee1bc8" target="e_7ee1ff4a70457dd7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be considered</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5bd74d0360e2f53b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Both the database and the smart speaker it serves would be considered the vulnerable system if a vulnerability in that database leads to the malfunction of the smart speaker</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be considered</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be considered"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_d2bc1fd8b8c63e8d" source="e_96b21e596f0b3131" target="e_7d71f6b7f3df9b75"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be defined for System of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9f3b8ea0d6656d12</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C11</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When assessed in the environmental metric group only, the subsequent system impact may, in addition to the logical systems defined for System of Interest, also include impacts to humans</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be defined for System of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be defined for System of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_a896683726429aaf" source="e_664d5b9e60c68b47" target="e_8a7307f97709a377"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">include</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_52741b0a6a612fd6</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C11</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When assessed in the environmental metric group only, the subsequent system impact may, in addition to the logical systems defined for System of Interest, also include impacts to humans</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">include</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["include", "includes"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_f527269c0fb49af5" source="e_2079f7f0585a6a0c" target="e_88e64807c1335218"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be managed by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c75fca74beb1cc40</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C11</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This metric measures the impact to the confidentiality of the information managed by the system due to a successfully exploited vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be managed by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be managed by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_747b4d164519db25" source="e_fabb36a448bb30b7" target="e_eb1797b298a230c0"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">disclosed</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_383901152199d84a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C11</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Alternatively, access to only some restricted information is obtained, but the disclosed information presents a direct, serious impact</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">disclosed</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["disclosed"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_240fe4e013d9bff7" source="e_d2b630e61129d09b" target="e_7ee1ff4a70457dd7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be protected by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9e6483e3bbfa4a7b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C12</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, the attacker is able to modify any/all files protected by the Vulnerable System</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be protected by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be protected by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_00b552d761ea89c4" source="e_d2b630e61129d09b" target="e_546996a8b2a435a8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be protected by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ae1321a5b54e25f9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C12</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, the attacker is able to modify any/all files protected by the Subsequent System</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be protected by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be protected by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_5bfa572fd26a280d" source="e_301c0352802feb18" target="e_2228b2b192c550b5"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be resulting from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_86f18c26050e2657</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This metric measures the impact to the availability of the impacted system resulting from a successfully exploited vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be resulting from</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be resulting from"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_d5ceef0c1e981c63" source="e_dfd2e098a96fa540" target="e_53dd9263602ab61d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">apply to loss of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7ae5701cfe4359e5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">While the Confidentiality and Integrity impact metrics apply to the loss of confidentiality or integrity of data (e.g., information, files) used by the system, this metric refers to the loss of availability of the impacted system itself, such as a networked service (e.g., web, database, email)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">apply to loss of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["apply to loss of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_0eca08e294f017be" source="e_09f091e141fb1fa3" target="e_53dd9263602ab61d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">apply to loss of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4854335c4eef9ab0</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">While the Confidentiality and Integrity impact metrics apply to the loss of confidentiality or integrity of data (e.g., information, files) used by the system, this metric refers to the loss of availability of the impacted system itself, such as a networked service (e.g., web, database, email)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">apply to loss of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["apply to loss of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_d84977c8c85fb009" source="e_61641163de7ce9bc" target="e_93d8650fe6b85a54"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d28a1e99a40baf21</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">While the Confidentiality and Integrity impact metrics apply to the loss of confidentiality or integrity of data (e.g., information, files) used by the system, this metric refers to the loss of availability of the impacted system itself, such as a networked service (e.g., web, database, email)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be used by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be used by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_54f630851dd431a8" source="e_22e800482ee5b5fd" target="e_4058f076b2d4719d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">consume</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6762b1961be986eb</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Since availability refers to the accessibility of information resources, attacks that consume network bandwidth, processor cycles, or disk space all impact the availability of a system</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">consume</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["consume"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_97e01deb95ac3e15" source="e_e56e3d4771ca46d9" target="e_841d5cae8321003