ibility of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_49dcecc1e899103a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Since availability refers to the accessibility of information resources, attacks that consume network bandwidth, processor cycles, or disk space all impact the availability of a system</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">refers to accessibility of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["refers to accessibility of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_779f4bb17e2c8805" source="e_d8d9b706557f592e" target="e_fbbdf1417a7b6e3e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be deny</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0638a018dacc1c2c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Even if repeated exploitation of the vulnerability is possible, the attacker does not have the ability to completely deny service to legitimate users</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be deny</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be deny"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_c40256467be5fbd2" source="e_d8d9b706557f592e" target="e_9111a79bb0a0398b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be deny</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f6750b4259eda130</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Even if repeated exploitation of the vulnerability is possible, the attacker does not have the ability to completely deny service to legitimate users</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be deny</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be deny"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_e8c04aea7b4e92d0" source="e_b02545dbef6b631f" target="e_ee6b44aab89ae669"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">measure</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f384c2922e810c55</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Threat metrics measure the current state of exploit techniques or code availability for a vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">measure</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["measure", "measures"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_1cf0e44a9185f1f2" source="e_b02545dbef6b631f" target="e_1d5201ae87cbebb9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">measure current state of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d0a6e6622f6b7e86</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Threat metrics measure the current state of exploit techniques or code availability for a vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">measure current state of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["measure current state of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_903d45d1d446a1c9" source="e_0a74ab6b8c124112" target="e_0f0dfafa6203250d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">progress from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3363e3d0241b4996</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Furthermore, the available exploit code or instructions may progress from a proof-of-concept demonstration to exploit code that is successful in exploiting the vulnerability consistently</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">progress from</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["progress from"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_fc543cc19ccda248" source="e_b4d9ea419ffeaae2" target="e_0f0dfafa6203250d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">progress from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4b9a27967fe31951</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Furthermore, the available exploit code or instructions may progress from a proof-of-concept demonstration to exploit code that is successful in exploiting the vulnerability consistently</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">progress from</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["progress from"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_4610d80e52583934" source="e_b88ca6e73460d909" target="e_c7cc5f5402d8a093"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be based on</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a7aeb47bd9055df1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">It is the responsibility of the CVSS consumer to populate the values of Exploit Maturity (E) based on information regarding the availability of exploitation code/processes and the state of exploitation techniques</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be based on</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be based on"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_cf0d0cbf3ebb25ac" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_d800caf744b5709e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is responsibility of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b5e34636509bbe1f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">It is the responsibility of the CVSS consumer to populate the values of Exploit Maturity (E) based on information regarding the availability of exploitation code/processes and the state of exploitation techniques</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is responsibility of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is responsibility of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_b1d25ec87712c992" source="e_1acae121d088630c" target="e_70d113b7cf439f46"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be preferred over those with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_96606e4b2b64a5c2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C15</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Operational Recommendation: Threat intelligence sources that provide Exploit Maturity information for all vulnerabilities should be preferred over those with only partial coverage</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be preferred over those with</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be preferred over those with"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_b898c9c329cd2cd9" source="e_b39009419fada99a" target="e_4d8f9e8bdafd1675"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is determined by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_43beb56738454482</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C16</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The full effect on the environmental score is determined by the corresponding Modified Base Impact metrics</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is determined by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is determined by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_ce52ea5a7d8542b8" source="e_768bf52735c34131" target="e_c89e9873faad3f01"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are set to default value of Defined reasonable worst case of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0525cb89d614bbf8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C16</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Following the concept of assuming “reasonable worst case”, in absence of explicit values, these metrics are set to the default value of Not Defined (X), which is equivalent to the metric value of High (H)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are set to default value of Defined reasonable worst case of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are set to default value of Defined reasonable worst case of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_8161ec2f3117e7f5" source="e_0dd1d2b00920b892" target="e_9b301e09540d09fc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is determined by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f4936dcfd9613c75</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C16</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The full effect on the resulting score is determined by the corresponding Base metrics as follows</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is determined by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is determined by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_6a1acc1284a51d29" source="e_596a3f18c38132af" target="e_db5858cf6e7acd99"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be represent</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2c0217abc14306d8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">It is acceptable to use the modified metrics to represent situations that increase the resulting score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be represent</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be represent"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_48bbc336fef1a9ac" source="e_db5858cf6e7acd99" target="e_754fa75553fa09be"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">increase</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0858144ce9ba8616</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">It is acceptable to use the modified metrics to represent situations that increase the resulting score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">increase</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["increase"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_5a8d5ae91a584e00" source="e_9b8d436553ded0d6" target="e_9299086080c4accc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be granted by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_05220323cf69f6e5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">However, in the consumer analyst’s environment, administrative privileges might be granted by default without authenticating the user</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be granted by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be granted by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_fc9a6ef2fa495f60" source="e_9b8d436553ded0d6" target="e_2b564a610fc97c2c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be granted by default in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c6265ac0af3c2637</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">However, in the consumer analyst’s environment, administrative privileges might be granted by default without authenticating the user</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be granted by default in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be granted by default in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_42747a23d14fff0f" source="e_9b8d436553ded0d6" target="e_e4f2a12429d15623"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be granted by default without</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c5fd395017d4d531</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">However, in the consumer analyst’s environment, administrative privileges might be granted by default without authenticating the user</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be granted by default without</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be granted by default without"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_c781f141f0c3ffca" source="e_f6498126c94c6f96" target="e_506193cfefade053"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">set</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7a0dd07abbdd1d36</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The analyst can set Privileges Required to High and Modified Privileges Required to None to reflect this more serious condition in their particular environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">set</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["set"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_c99506b013721a39" source="e_f6498126c94c6f96" target="e_8baba9b928c90883"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">set</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c0848489badee2e8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The analyst can set Privileges Required to High and Modified Privileges Required to None to reflect this more serious condition in their particular environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">set</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["set"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_b09532e0581ab610" source="e_6cb481a83536ac29" target="e_f90f01579634abed"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be Required to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d193a02456c510ec</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The analyst can set Privileges Required to High and Modified Privileges Required to None to reflect this more serious condition in their particular environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be Required to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be Required to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_2528a9a1c76c6011" source="e_cbda6adb410f4617" target="e_f90f01579634abed"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be Required to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b29c6b78acb56f43</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The analyst can set Privileges Required to High and Modified Privileges Required to None to reflect this more serious condition in their particular environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be Required to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be Required to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_86d0a0cc3b6c946a" source="e_d45a29c5219856c1" target="e_24724c67123f239d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be to run listening service with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_db32ab40eb771690</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Example 2: The default configuration for a vulnerable system may be to run a listening service with administrator privileges, for which a compromise might grant an attacker Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability impacts that are all High</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be to run listening service with</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be to run listening service with"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_9c9c2f9695feb2d2" source="e_d45a29c5219856c1" target="e_349144947774f114"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be to run</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4eea76259d22783f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Example 2: The default configuration for a vulnerable system may be to run a listening service with administrator privileges, for which a compromise might grant an attacker Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability impacts that are all High</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be to run</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be to run"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_0c08d204b0952ef3" source="e_2777340d458412d6" target="e_24724c67123f239d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">grant attacker Confidentiality listening service with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_110095d42457583d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Example 2: The default configuration for a vulnerable system may be to run a listening service with administrator privileges, for which a compromise might grant an attacker Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability impacts that are all High</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">grant attacker Confidentiality listening service with</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["grant attacker Confidentiality listening service with"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_f79cedb1d9de7417" source="e_2777340d458412d6" target="e_349144947774f114"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">grant attacker Confidentiality</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e6812a99763259c6</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Example 2: The default configuration for a vulnerable system may be to run a listening service with administrator privileges, for which a compromise might grant an attacker Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability impacts that are all High</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">grant attacker Confidentiality</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["grant attacker Confidentiality"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_5f0c2e35be99a6d7" source="e_2cbef1015e8443fb" target="e_040dc8c7ec38f443"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be running with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f84dcfd54de1b504</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Yet, in the consumer analyst’s environment, that same Internet service might be running with reduced privileges; in that case, the Modified Confidentiality, Modified Integrity, and Modified Availability might each be set to Low</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be running with</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be running with"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_3bc1e9b2b0cbea52" source="e_a00feff6fcb1c982" target="e_b35718531dfb7863"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">uses</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c80eef9512a5e8d5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Not Defined is the default and uses the metric value of the associated Base metric</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">use</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["use", "uses", "do use", "Uses"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_edfb3ac1a477e8cd" source="e_87a35caaa98faf5a" target="e_cd7fcb8a4781c41f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">result in injuries categorized as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0b35fa4f4e7b137e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Safety impact is applicable when it is predictable that an exploited vulnerability may result in injuries categorized as Marginal or worse using the IEC 61508 definitions outlined in the chart below</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">result in injuries categorized as</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["result in injuries categorized as"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_fa00f6e3ce900a86" source="e_87a35caaa98faf5a" target="e_8a528e0b3c3195da"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">result in injuries categorized as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b3a8980acc459963</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Safety impact is applicable when it is predictable that an exploited vulnerability may result in injuries categorized as Marginal or worse using the IEC 61508 definitions outlined in the chart below</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">result in injuries categorized as</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["result in injuries categorized as"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_3b6e584c224e58de" source="e_d5f0963a1e0287ed" target="e_cd7fcb8a4781c41f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be categorized as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a77df8b802f6a2f7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Safety impact is applicable when it is predictable that an exploited vulnerability may result in injuries categorized as Marginal or worse using the IEC 61508 definitions outlined in the chart below</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be categorized as</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be categorized as"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_83b6eb4f60476a6e" source="e_d5f0963a1e0287ed" target="e_8a528e0b3c3195da"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be categorized as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6b20a7a5a00053dd</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Safety impact is applicable when it is predictable that an exploited vulnerability may result in injuries categorized as Marginal or worse using the IEC 61508 definitions outlined in the chart below</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be categorized as</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be categorized as"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_1dda2edbfa1354ba" source="e_469e1f0a792f149b" target="e_371e2a8932c3cb22"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are leveraged in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7c756b772b673633</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Note: Safety metric values are leveraged in both the Supplemental Metric Group (provided by the assessment providers) and the Environmental Metric Group (provided by the consumer analyst)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are leveraged in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are leveraged in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_01d1ab6d651a9e91" source="e_469e1f0a792f149b" target="e_b84ee762ce82df1d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are leveraged in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b0af087854a3d016</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Note: Safety metric values are leveraged in both the Supplemental Metric Group (provided by the assessment providers) and the Environmental Metric Group (provided by the consumer analyst)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are leveraged in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are leveraged in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_6fe5bb4cf354564f" source="e_54b478dcf9b37c22" target="e_1e8070a280814846"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">provides</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1e4e5c9ff3122f22</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A new, optional metric group called the Supplemental metric group provides new metrics that describe and measure additional extrinsic attributes of a vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">provides</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["provides", "provide"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_6d4980859b5b2714" source="e_290d8da624d84fb0" target="e_9ab722c5f7b8353b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">see</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b87c8601faa34b2b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Suppliers and vendors (AKA: scoring providers) may or may not provide Safety as a Supplemental Metric as they see fit</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">see</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["see"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_5d461acc07cba05a" source="e_9cf9e67a33f313e5" target="e_d999ddd1227d98cb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be aligned to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_36a452fbfa9ef650</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When a system does have an intended use or fitness of purpose aligned to safety, it is possible that exploiting a vulnerability within that system may have Safety impact which can be represented in the Supplemental Metrics group</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be aligned to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be aligned to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_83e335e87638eab5" source="e_fb8ea41b8705c2d6" target="e_8fc389924516130b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be represented in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_14de90c77e147f2d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When a system does have an intended use or fitness of purpose aligned to safety, it is possible that exploiting a vulnerability within that system may have Safety impact which can be represented in the Supplemental Metrics group</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be represented in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be represented in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_2872700f18657803" source="e_35187791756c46dc" target="e_79a5b245db4e61f6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9cec10eca500f4ee</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The possible values for the Safety Supplemental Metric are as follows:</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are as</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are as"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_12e1bbe334a48f52" source="e_d999ddd1227d98cb" target="e_c58642aeeaa4024e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be described</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_331d80fee366ef35</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As a Supplemental metric, and consistent with the above table, Safety can be described with metric values of S:X, S:P, or S:N</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be described</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be described"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_e0df4fc6cba6fcfc" source="e_d999ddd1227d98cb" target="e_000918bc13dd8c22"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be described consistent with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4369732790b01ea2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As a Supplemental metric, and consistent with the above table, Safety can be described with metric values of S:X, S:P, or S:N</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be described consistent with</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be described consistent with"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_f0d43a830b796f0b" source="e_d1a2cdb8457da1b4" target="e_2e115427b410e854"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">captures answer to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_019c067ad7761f1f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The “Automatable” metric captures the answer to the question ”Can an attacker automate exploitation events for this vulnerability across multiple targets?” based on steps 1-4 of the kill chain2 [Hutchins et al., 2011]</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">captures answer to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["captures answer to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_fc0d9627a3589064" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_3c092a597518507c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">automate exploitation events for vulnerability across</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1f61b31aefedbc29</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The “Automatable” metric captures the answer to the question ”Can an attacker automate exploitation events for this vulnerability across multiple targets?” based on steps 1-4 of the kill chain2 [Hutchins et al., 2011]</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">automate exploitation events for vulnerability across</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["automate exploitation events for vulnerability across"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_fcaaa508fe19987e" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_cd0eecf6d03be185"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">automate</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_120b193e2d0bb1b7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The “Automatable” metric captures the answer to the question ”Can an attacker automate exploitation events for this vulnerability across multiple targets?” based on steps 1-4 of the kill chain2 [Hutchins et al., 2011]</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">automate</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["automate"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_e1c9808e57776f12" source="e_bb192ae9e03fa1fb" target="e_4a17d33b79767a98"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be incorporate</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b432f097951ed828</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C20</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">To facilitate a standardized method to incorporate additional provider-supplied assessment, an optional “pass-through” Supplemental Metric called Provider Urgency is available</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be incorporate</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be incorporate"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_96d23c4130861a28" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_d9b1236e8a068718"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">gain control over with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_094e0eae180d408f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C20</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Value Density describes the resources that the attacker will gain control over with a single exploitation event</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">gain control over with</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["gain control over with"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_f7b35ec8bcfdc266" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_ba719f9de4e00ae9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">gain</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9de81cf5d094c2d5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C20</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Value Density describes the resources that the attacker will gain control over with a single exploitation event</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">gain</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["gain"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_d5e44918572ac2e1" source="e_a2795c20852a50cd" target="e_c9e58d685e4a9f95"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are direct responsibility of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_caa076a93354189f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C21</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Heuristically, such systems are often the direct responsibility of “system operators” rather than users</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are direct responsibility of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are direct responsibility of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_8ff267e21199ec5d" source="e_f7f0082982beecc7" target="e_fd676437ab51b484"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">to provide</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_74cc442fc46ddd3a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C21</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The intention of the Vulnerability Response Effort metric is to provide supplemental information on how difficult it is for consumers to provide an initial response to the impact of vulnerabilities for deployed products and services in their infrastructure</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">to provide</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["to provide"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_1a1645ec4263d533" source="e_f7f0082982beecc7" target="e_fa83bcbab886e89f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">to provide</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5b7755d83264abb3</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C21</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The intention of the Vulnerability Response Effort metric is to provide supplemental information on how difficult it is for consumers to provide an initial response to the impact of vulnerabilities for deployed products and services in their infrastructure</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">to provide</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["to provide"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_c33103a61adcb1d2" source="e_70973f0fc94d31c9" target="e_7f765772ac6c1cb7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be required into consideration when</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8b404bd3336768ff</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C21</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The consumer can then take this additional information on effort required into consideration when applying mitigations and/or scheduling remediation</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be required into consideration when</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be required into consideration when"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_f48b39394244274f" source="e_70973f0fc94d31c9" target="e_301ab130bb3a8852"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be required into consideration when</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9883aad3607bba30</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C21</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The consumer can then take this additional information on effort required into consideration when applying mitigations and/or scheduling remediation</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be required into consideration when</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be required into consideration when"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_df2781848461b0e6" source="e_70973f0fc94d31c9" target="e_d93d3f2293801306"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be required into</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4959632157eb961e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C21</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The consumer can then take this additional information on effort required into consideration when applying mitigations and/or scheduling remediation</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be required into</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be required into"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_6c3a9875f58a17f6" source="e_23ea030c6b50d6f1" target="e_d7deb00ec419ff44"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">involves</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_89ee9f27239da5c5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The only resolution to the vulnerability involves physical replacement (e.g. units deployed would have to be recalled for a depot level repair or replacement)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">involve</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["involve", "involves"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_2cba2fc509e6ebb2" source="e_47eab5f20c539cdb" target="e_ac4fee6dcc702b89"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">have to be recalled for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_61f99f39994284c1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The only resolution to the vulnerability involves physical replacement (e.g. units deployed would have to be recalled for a depot level repair or replacement)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">have to be recalled for</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["have to be recalled for"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_7cfcd66d4b71e910" source="e_47eab5f20c539cdb" target="e_524736485bb389af"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">have to be recalled for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4af8dac6f2f16a69</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The only resolution to the vulnerability involves physical replacement (e.g. units deployed would have to be recalled for a depot level repair or replacement)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">have to be recalled for</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["have to be recalled for"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_f40d7e6b95c04ed6" source="e_290d8da624d84fb0" target="e_2e1496c46b0c67cc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">help</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2211c1215b9efe4e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">They are intended to help organizations properly assess and prioritize their vulnerability management processes</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">help</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["help"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_bca6c30b99714661" source="e_290d8da624d84fb0" target="e_40e21c1bf87487d6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">help</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b7eb153ce241f478</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">They are intended to help organizations properly assess and prioritize their vulnerability management processes</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">help</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["help"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_e092d53b0d634a8c" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_3871d9a29382ae85"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is used to record CVSS metric information in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_396f564b9d894e0b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">It is commonly used to record or transfer CVSS metric information in a concise and machine-readable form</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is used to record CVSS metric information in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is used to record CVSS metric information in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_ed98e8e7667774d8" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_c3091b917bf6c37c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is used to record CVSS metric information in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5022ded5f576f588</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">It is commonly used to record or transfer CVSS metric information in a concise and machine-readable form</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is used to record CVSS metric information in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is used to record CVSS metric information in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_97bed250d0a2b286" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_11d9e0f2a7ae327b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is used to record</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_24041d413fab48b3</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">It is commonly used to record or transfer CVSS metric information in a concise and machine-readable form</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is used to record</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is used to record"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_913d3c7441987fbb" source="e_9e8758f7636f5ca5" target="e_534c943c598a31b3"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are defined</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4b6308422efdc0d9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The abbreviated forms are defined earlier in this specification (in parentheses after each metric name and metric value, case sensitive), and are summarized in the table below</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are defined</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are defined", "defined", "has defined"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_58e49d296838f8ef" source="e_075097bc32ffa89f" target="e_afccd7a4fc5871a9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are considered to have value of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4cd9ecef4a3f2bfd</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C23</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Threat, Environmental, and Supplemental metrics are optional, and omitted metrics are considered to have the value of Not Defined (X)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are considered to have value of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are considered to have value of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_112cb932feb9809f" source="e_8c5bdfed19c88e1e" target="e_97d5b9fcbb9ac78b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be included in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_14cd379067b847bf</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C23</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Metrics with a value of Not Defined can be explicitly included in a vector string if desired</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be included in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be included in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_73eb5481e9107f97" source="e_5f88e862f178ae99" target="e_e7e4cc3411114886"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">represents boundary between qualitative severity scores to be</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_18d9e22138d6dc8c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C24</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Solicit expert opinion to decide which equivalence set of vectors p in the ordering of vectors represents the boundary between qualitative severity scores to be backwards compatible with qualitative severity score boundaries from CVSS v3.x</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">represents boundary between qualitative severity scores to be</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["represents boundary between qualitative severity scores to be"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_8c3661fc9df52e2c" source="e_5f88e862f178ae99" target="e_81f749c9c181f2c3"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">represents boundary between qualitative severity scores to be</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_05c8772d759405a1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C24</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Solicit expert opinion to decide which equivalence set of vectors p in the ordering of vectors represents the boundary between qualitative severity scores to be backwards compatible with qualitative severity score boundaries from CVSS v3.x</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">represents boundary between qualitative severity scores to be</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["represents boundary between qualitative severity scores to be"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_218c943605a75d22" source="e_5f88e862f178ae99" target="e_1276ee29f118b2a1"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">represents boundary between qualitative severity scores to be</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6ca519b7734c5549</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C24</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Solicit expert opinion to decide which equivalence set of vectors p in the ordering of vectors represents the boundary between qualitative severity scores to be backwards compatible with qualitative severity score boundaries from CVSS v3.x</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">represents boundary between qualitative severity scores to be</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["represents boundary between qualitative severity scores to be"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_253aff6541ca2bbd" source="e_bfaf17725bfcbe42" target="e_b52de94b00055efe"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">adjusts scores of vectors within qualitatively equivalent set of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a7315629c4a616e9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C24</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Create a small score modification factor that adjusts the scores of vectors within a qualitatively equivalent set of vectors so that a change of any metric value results in a resulting score change, where possible</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">adjusts scores of vectors within qualitatively equivalent set of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["adjusts scores of vectors within qualitatively equivalent set of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_3172acb396c6e8cb" source="e_bfaf17725bfcbe42" target="e_b52de94b00055efe"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">adjusts scores of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9aecaeb373d3e386</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C24</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Create a small score modification factor that adjusts the scores of vectors within a qualitatively equivalent set of vectors so that a change of any metric value results in a resulting score change, where possible</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">adjusts scores of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["adjusts scores of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_83eaa6ee6f8d28e5" source="e_9bdb10fbcabccec2" target="e_4909cad877ba4cb8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is larger than</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e15fd416cff6f51b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C24</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The intent is that the score change is not larger than the uncertainty in the ranking of the vector groups as collected from the expert comparison data in step 2</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is larger than</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is larger than"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_bba3c7f9de4bdd3c" source="e_87304ba0c995dfd8" target="e_a1855c7c1104c724"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">provides</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0e9ffb9ec87073c6</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C25</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The CVSS v4.0 formula provides a mathematical approximation of all possible metric combinations ranked in order of severity where vectors are clustered in sets called MacroVectors</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">provides</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["provides", "provide"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_54e14aa520ffa544" source="e_3c6f55c088fab9eb" target="e_b61076f91213a657"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">determined following preliminary metrics subgroups</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c68f8797d9e68c67</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C25</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">To determine a preliminary set of relevant MacroVectors, The SIG determined the following preliminary metrics subgroups</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">determined following preliminary metrics subgroups</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["determined following preliminary metrics subgroups"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_7025a7a153304b55" source="e_290d8da624d84fb0" target="e_e376508129b912c3"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be considered</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_fba25b2bf6294211</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C25</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Since EQ3 and EQ6 are not independent they must be considered together</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be considered</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be considered"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_9f337b7de204725a" source="e_43ffce3506ce7430" target="e_f244b68cb5567ebc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">satisfy</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2cc8e2a2481bddd7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C25</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example the MacroVectors which satisfy EQ1 at level 1 shown in Table 24 have as highest severity vectors all vectors with</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">satisfy</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["satisfy"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_cccc716f58eb5149" source="e_c0ce3e1fa2075260" target="e_9d702092532e5aae"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is assigned score of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a716aae400fc58f9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C27</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The highest severity vector of a MacroVector is always assigned the score of the MacroVector from the cvss_lookup.js file within the CVSS v4.0 calculator reference implementation available on GitHub (see Section 8.3)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is assigned score of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is assigned score of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_6452b42d91ca66ab" source="e_c0ce3e1fa2075260" target="e_3bfabacd58fbea1f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is assigned score of MacroVector from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_fb3b32c9cecdce8e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C27</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The highest severity vector of a MacroVector is always assigned the score of the MacroVector from the cvss_lookup.js file within the CVSS v4.0 calculator reference implementation available on GitHub (see Section 8.3)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is assigned score of MacroVector from</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is assigned score of MacroVector from"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_0bb9d40b397301a8" source="e_5ad2f2ffe7c97896" target="e_b8800f698321cdcb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is determined by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6957d0429bfcf77d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C27</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The proportion of the distance is determined by dividing the severity distance of the to-be-scored vector by the depth of the MacroVector</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is determined by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is determined by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_e68ad623698059e7" source="e_aea8700531f30f00" target="e_43db8c6b67ae0647"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is multiplied by proportion of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_da7b8e27f541237c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C27</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The maximal scoring difference is multiplied by the proportion of distance</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is multiplied by proportion of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is multiplied by proportion of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_dfd3979e8b5a8813" source="e_401168aab527b720" target="e_6332c5e3343e7bc8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is score of MacroVector i.e. score of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_11173e9118c5023d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C27</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The score of the vector is the score of the MacroVector (i.e. the score of the highest severity vector) minus the mean distance so computed</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><dat