e group represents the intrinsic qualities of a vulnerability that are constant over time and across user environments, the Threat group reflects the characteristics of a vulnerability that change over time, and the Environmental group represents the characteristics of a vulnerability that are unique to a user's environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">change over</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["change over", "changes over", "do change over"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_782227d72686cec3" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_44fb585ec7e6699b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are unique to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_93f60c92733af721</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Base group represents the intrinsic qualities of a vulnerability that are constant over time and across user environments, the Threat group reflects the characteristics of a vulnerability that change over time, and the Environmental group represents the characteristics of a vulnerability that are unique to a user's environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are unique to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are unique to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_20faadae1d917365" source="e_38c8318b1fef3eff" target="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">represents intrinsic qualities of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_aefa7a619c118837</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51<