ce_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A CVSS vector string consists of a compressed textual representation of the values used to derive the score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">consists of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["consists of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_9bd4c21103f00c4b" source="e_a9ed604eb1323e31" target="e_4364e67a28b13c95"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used to derive</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_335c07558374e6e6</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A CVSS vector string consists of a compressed textual representation of the values used to derive the score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be used to derive</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be used to derive"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_f6245f72706e46e0" source="e_768bf52735c34131" target="e_f8b520c0a0b6460f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used to calculate</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_da8ea0ee09aa2473</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Numerical CVSS Scores have very different meanings based on the metrics used to calculate them</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be used to calculate</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be used to calculate"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_7569d7010f731631" source="e_768bf52735c34131" target="e_bbcb8ea999353380"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4b5cdd2a45bccbdc</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Therefore, numerical CVSS scores should be enumerated using nomenclature that communicates the metrics used in its generation</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be used in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be used in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_dc99f60e8e7960d2" source="e_9e3f8e0349f649b1" target="e_d800caf744b5709e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is responsibility of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_93be65285afe6051</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The application of Environmental and Threat metrics is the responsibility of the CVSS consumer</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is responsibility of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is responsibility of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_40d367bfe0bf8647" source="e_845db19a5f318ea7" target="e_d800caf744b5709e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is responsibility of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_904b5b6c5c12f2d1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The application of Environmental and Threat metrics is the responsibility of the CVSS consumer</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is responsibility of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is responsibility of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_6db846cbbb2cd2d7" source="e_0aeb5fdf6effbdc8" target="e_51321b750147cbd0"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be enumerated as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0ad4c0032e4effbd</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Assessment providers such as product maintainers and other public/private entities such as the National Vulnerability Database (NVD) typically provide only the Base Scores enumerated as CVSS-B</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be enumerated as</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be enumerated as"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_30caebb7bf97ef5f" source="e_ba6a59ae6b0db851" target="e_5e3014756335417a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">result in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7be1f0fbc2f8f739</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The absence of explicit Threat and/or Environmental metric selections will still result in a complete score using default (“Not Defined”) values</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">result in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["result in", "resulted in", "results in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_d060d74da4941f4b" source="e_0b1f826002e28a94" target="e_5e3014756335417a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">result in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d0e199b08c0ea063</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The absence of explicit Threat and/or Environmental metric selections will still result in a complete score using default (“Not Defined”) values</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">result in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["result in", "resulted in", "results in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_11ff3c040633b469" source="e_228b54a1a94571c6" target="e_8fc1e9fb6e48faf5"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has been updated</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c8a3cd5895e80681</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The CVSS Specification Document has been updated to emphasize and clarify the fact that CVSS Base (CVSS-B) scores are designed to measure the severity of a vulnerability and should not be used alone to assess risk</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">has been updated</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["has been updated"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_bc6ff05703ef4c35" source="e_2b936a70397531bf" target="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are designed to measure severity of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_fdda8542d1a4b16e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The CVSS Specification Document has been updated to emphasize and clarify the fact that CVSS Base (CVSS-B) scores are designed to measure the severity of a vulnerability and should not be used alone to assess risk</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are designed to measure severity of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are designed to measure severity of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_65423931c1c20e96" source="e_2979a68b0d157ffd" target="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">represents intrinsic characteristics of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_78639fd464af970c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The CVSS v4.0 Specification Document clearly states that the CVSS Base Score represents only the intrinsic characteristics of a vulnerability and is independent of any factor associated with threat or the computing environment where the vulnerable system resides</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">represents intrinsic characteristics of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["represents intrinsic characteristics of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_ed90f6ed7bdb70be" source="e_7ee1ff4a70457dd7" target="e_8b98ab92d36f0036"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">resides</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_383ae85b9587f5fd</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The CVSS v4.0 Specification Document clearly states that the CVSS Base Score represents only the intrinsic characteristics of a vulnerability and is independent of any factor associated with threat or the computing environment where the vulnerable system resides</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">resides</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["resides"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_4da6a906d3d45577" source="e_2979a68b0d157ffd" target="e_106a49c8576bc28c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be supplemented with analysis of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_61f86d59f01b001b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The CVSS Base Score should be supplemented with an analysis of the environment (Environmental Metrics), and with attributes that may change over time (Threat Metrics)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be supplemented with analysis of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be supplemented with analysis of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_88cfd9773d3c2088" source="e_29c85f9f417d06f8" target="e_ca335c133f4134dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">change over</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_83924bbf10f0ff5c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The CVSS Base Score should be supplemented with an analysis of the environment (Environmental Metrics), and with attributes that may change over time (Threat Metrics)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">change over</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["change over", "changes over", "do change over"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_4fe6101f664c285d" source="e_5a896e5dd7fb3b56" target="e_b14fc5adc67ef919"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be considered</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4a99451e7974f7a6</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For an organization that employ