e">The additional metrics allow industry sectors such as privacy, automotive, etc., to assess factors that are outside the core CVSS standard</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be assess</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be assess"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_18284cf0eaa34ec6" source="e_8e874df517877380" target="e_50b2ccaf2cca5963"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are outside</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4a18dd8f69f5eae9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The additional metrics allow industry sectors such as privacy, automotive, etc., to assess factors that are outside the core CVSS standard</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are outside</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are outside"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_5b904168ebe6b91c" source="e_3268c0d3caf6f382" target="e_e7e4cc3411114886"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">represents boundary between qualitative severity scores to be</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f84e13f9c4ee9180</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Solicit expert opinion to decide what vector group in the ordering of vectors represents the boundary between qualitative severity scores to be backwards compatible with qualitative severity score boundaries from CVSS v3.x</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">represents boundary between qualitative severity scores to be</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["represents boundary between qualitative severity scores to be"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_3957e8ed9e9d4010" source="e_3268c0d3caf6f382" target="e_81f749c9c181f2c3"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">represents boundary between qualitative severity scores to be</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3cbbcaa7aff51f23</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Solicit expert opinion to decide what vector group in the ordering of vectors represents the boundary between qualitative severity scores to be backwards compatible with qualitative severity score boundaries from CVSS v3.x</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">represents boundary between qualitative severity scores to be</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["represents boundary between qualitative severity scores to be"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_7ce40d9596c17c88" source="e_3268c0d3caf6f382" target="e_1276ee29f118b2a1"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">represents boundary between qualitative severity scores to be</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_dba0c3078943caf1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Solicit expert opinion to decide what vector group in the ordering of vectors represents the boundary between qualitative severity scores to be backwards compatible with qualitative severity score boundaries from CVSS v3.x</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">represents boundary between qualitative severity scores to be</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["represents boundary between qualitative severity scores to be"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_5d39aec1915e8fdb" source="e_bfaf17725bfcbe42" target="e_97a865b3178655c7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">adjusts scores of vectors within</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_fbc4af3f01f93898</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Create a small score modification factor that adjusts the scores of vectors within a vector group so that a change of any metric value results in a score change</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">adjusts scores of vectors within</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["adjusts scores of vectors within"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_f594eac825aec42a" source="e_bfaf17725bfcbe42" target="e_b52de94b00055efe"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">adjusts scores of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_49ce8ac33f56ce93</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Create a small score modification factor that adjusts the scores of vectors within a vector group so that a change of any metric value results in a score change</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">adjusts scores of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["adjusts scores of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_d383424a8f1a6cbe" source="e_9bdb10fbcabccec2" target="e_4909cad877ba4cb8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is larger than</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4190390e1be90804</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The intent is that the score change is not larger than the uncertainty in the ranking of the vector groups as collected from the expert comparison data in step 2</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is larger than</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is larger than"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_723d28d93688c6fd" source="e_1ca2c11440c1c7d8" target="e_ae73db6c6dc9038f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">see</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_dcb472eb51b9f77d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Usually, the work grows in an order faster than the list size (in computational terms, order nlog(n), see Sorting algorithm - Wikipedia)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">see</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["see"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_3433fa5916fa2933" source="e_33dca876a41ad65c" target="e_d7273f4e25365f2d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be rated</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_10b5586dcd64fd7c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The bigger the point-score difference, the larger the chance the higher-scored vector would be rated as more severe</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be rated</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be rated"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_3a89576e9db11d50" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_25951c5d0a9e44bb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">believe</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_085e2c484a48c8e6</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Therefore, we believe the Elo algorithm output is stable and represents a reliable transformation from the diverse expert opinion inputs to a single severity ordering of the metric-group-based vector sets</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">believe</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["believe"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_1a039f3dfa1e82b0" source="e_e13aa03d5edf67fb" target="e_7292e4cff7ad0e72"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">define</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_cd10730b5621c2d1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">To do this, the SIG wanted to decide which metric-group-based vector sets define the qualitative severity set boundaries</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">define</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["define", "defines"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_fa0a990981d4f974" source="e_2e7f6508490301b8" target="e_a3f5a028c4073979"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">defined</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b4d305f514c7d544</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The SIG's then defined the boundaries as the average of the 5 SIG members' selections</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are defined</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are defined", "defined", "has defined"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_6199847f4c2012da" source="e_3b9aab84428344fa" target="e_37bc44e6064f36ed"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">resulted in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_38ee92ecd293ca26</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The result of the total ordering (step 3) and qualitative severity boundaries (step 4) resulted in the following number of metric-group-based vector sets in each qualitative severity value</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">result in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["result in", "resulted in", "results in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_eca7d3e94cc2f095" source="e_8ca3eb60be0618d3" target="e_d4e917125a7a8d5a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">share</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_dbb15dc8ac671255</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">That algorithm is agglomerative hierarchical clustering (Hierarchical clustering - Wikipedia), which makes sure that vector sets that share the same CVSS v4 BTE score also have the smallest difference between their Elo-point scores</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">share</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["share"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_e2df7ad7c9449458" source="e_57973dca3393636d" target="e_a705103665e9ea94"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be create</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e16a477b1c8a7a70</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In order to meet a requirement that any change in a metric value result in at least a 0.1 change in the CVSS v4 BTE score, the SIG added an additional step to create a small change in the score based on metric value changes within metric-group-based vector sets</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be create</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be create"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_257a945873a3a857" source="e_c983c1a036f2d485" target="e_a09a3298b7a4d470"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be based on</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c09423d820a2bf81</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Therefore, it is plausible to algorithmically define a change in CVSS v4 BTE score based on this ordering</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be based on</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be based on"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_7ebf3a9edadf42a7" source="e_0c097f4d339f6496" target="e_0fe865e6b0d11c6c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">was used to sort big-picture ordering of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0169d5cc21c62d91</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">That is, the expert opinion was used to sort the big-picture ordering of qualitatively important differences</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">was used to sort big-picture ordering of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["was used to sort big-picture ordering of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_bf88c02702f49028" source="e_39d80c497ea15938" target="e_f922a5468724441b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are salient to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_678b0666b666b468</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The small changes in metric value that are not salient to a metric-group-based equivalence set change can still be used to represent a small change in the score that is consistent with the Elo-point difference interpretation of how likely an expert is to rate one vector set as more severe than another</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are salient to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are salient to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_a17d89af8cbd86a7" source="e_43b908d08d2ede0c" target="e_f7f0082982beecc7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are number of recommendations for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e418ba26f35fa9c9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Below are a number of recommendations for consumers when assessing vulnerabilities with CVSS v4.0</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are number of recommendations for</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are number of recommendations for"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_e72598e9e7ee7519" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_31d865c1327d86e7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is recommended to enrich</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_311602c9bb9f3d04</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">It is highly recommended to enrich the results from vulnerability scanning solutions with asset data</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is recommended to enrich</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is recommended to enrich"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_22dfc5491b1c7196" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_c71e4952422c37b4"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is recommended to enrich</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1a0f2ad52a87e292</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">It is highly recommended to enrich the results from vulnerability scanning solutions with asset data</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is recommended to enrich</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is recommended to enrich"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_8fce2ae7fd0fd732" source="e_57e6975d8ca79e1f" target="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be integrated with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_544211315541fe6b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Often, asset management data is kept in a database that can easily be integrated with vulnerability scan data</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be integrated with</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be integrated with"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_41ab24420805b77b" source="e_8df5ed6835bb03e8" target="e_84b1db4e585f1e60"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be utilize Environmental Metric Group to improve quality of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d1c23edc60793de7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Not only will this step enable a Vulnerability Management team to utilize the Environmental Metric Group to improve the quality of the resulting CVSS scores, the engineers responsible for remediating identified vulnerabilities will have more information at their disposal</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be utilize Environmental Metric Group to improve quality of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be utilize Environmental Metric Group to improve quality of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_fd90304553194a1e" source="e_718734d165927d5b" target="e_d93d3f2293801306"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">takes environmental factors into</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e5515131dbe9c05e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Once this information is integrated using automation, the result is a CVSS-BE score that takes those environmental factors into consideration</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">takes environmental factors into</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["takes environmental factors into"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_b400d27c506c64c2" source="e_9f4bc004f1ab89c0" target="e_b49174ea90f56347"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">have been exploited which in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_fd6f7176817e3178</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Knowing which vulnerabilities have been exploited in the past should have a significant impact on the resulting score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">have been exploited which in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["have been exploited which in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_eb223e72f5f2fb72" source="e_ebf0ee816f3b1469" target="e_754fa75553fa09be"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">have significant impact on</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_04d62e5b2025965d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Knowing which vulnerabilities have been exploited in the past should have a significant impact on the resulting score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">have significant impact on</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["have significant impact on"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_c29fcd6467fe0935" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_1ee64bd510d4d512"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is recommended to gather</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_522cd262e27c6bb7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">It is important to understand that none of these sources are perfect and it is highly recommended to gather multiple sources of threat intelligence to improve the comprehensiveness and fidelity of the information being used to enrich your vulnerability data</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is recommended to gather</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is recommended to gather"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_b04de0c68b3965e7" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_85409dcf567a6c20"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is recommended to gather</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c333aed85e1811f2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">It is important to understand that none of these sources are perfect and it is highly recommended to gather multiple sources of threat intelligence to improve the comprehensiveness and fidelity of the information being used to enrich your vulnerability data</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is recommended to gather</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is recommended to gather"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_50e979b2d3baaede" source="e_d4cff6070f136c90" target="e_35b2194131dcbc9a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">constrain impacts to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_12e26522f9283bb8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When understanding when to assess the impact of vulnerabilities, analysts should constrain impacts to a reasonable, final outcome which they are confident an attacker is able to achieve</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">constrain impacts to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["constrain impacts to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_7c9ad5080d8bd5ff" source="e_d4cff6070f136c90" target="e_57598c70746601d2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">constrain</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ab04af7a