count (assume that the attacker could log out from their own account and log back in as root):</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">issue</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["issue"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_47c5ce89e416ee3d" source="e_f6498126c94c6f96" target="e_cff67433523aab4e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">issue commands as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ceadb31275c30ed9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Gaining access to this password represents a direct, serious loss of Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability because the analyst can reasonably issue commands as the root / administrator account (assume that the attacker could log out from their own account and log back in as root):</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">issue commands as</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["issue commands as"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_ac14f6c9368f3dc3" source="e_a982d11f5c7cd47c" target="e_df2e46d7bc1804f4"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be assume</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d48085892f19d83d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Gaining access to this password represents a direct, serious loss of Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability because the analyst can reasonably issue commands as the root / administrator account (assume that the attacker could log out from their own account and log back in as root):</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be assume</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be assume"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_17ca95b14da683c6" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_b1dbc907aabf08ed"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">log out from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_af4bedd204d7b6d8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Gaining access to this password represents a direct, serious loss of Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability because the analyst can reasonably issue commands as the root / administrator account (assume that the attacker could log out from their own account and log back in as root):</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">log out from</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["log out from"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_8020a91dd9b24bfc" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_b1dbc907aabf08ed"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">log out from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e7a6ecf1423aacec</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">/ administrator account (assume that the attacker could log out from their own account and log back in as root):</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">log out from</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["log out from"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_ee964a8ad2747f27" source="e_61641163de7ce9bc" target="e_9111a79bb0a0398b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2febb7ecaf318bd6</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Confidentiality and Integrity metrics refer to impacts that affect the data used by the service</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be used by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be used by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_850baa62b395f9c1" source="e_d4cff6070f136c90" target="e_571bc10d653316b8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">assess</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ffdfe917dd2e84d4</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Specifically, analysts should only assess Network or Adjacent when a vulnerability is bound to the network stack</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">assess</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["assess"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_cae8ed99dd303f02" source="e_d4cff6070f136c90" target="e_acf7de49bb06f2fb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">assess</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_578aeea70cf80eec</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Specifically, analysts should only assess Network or Adjacent when a vulnerability is bound to the network stack</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">assess</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["assess"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_044d32d783927b92" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_f6498126c94c6f96"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is responsibility of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_767f3da6d742c877</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When assessing a chain of vulnerabilities, it is the responsibility of the analyst to identify which vulnerabilities are combined to form the chained resulting score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is responsibility of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is responsibility of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_b39725bc1251d252" source="e_9f4bc004f1ab89c0" target="e_8b9b96e6b76b1b6d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are combined which to form</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_05f6e0d90d59f6c5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When assessing a chain of vulnerabilities, it is the responsibility of the analyst to identify which vulnerabilities are combined to form the chained resulting score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are combined which to form</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are combined which to form"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_5bd8c3e8732103da" source="e_e163460c91338b08" target="e_5ad6c123e5abaf11"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be communicated within vulnerability disclosure notice For</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7c8a3723ad0142a0</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, this may be communicated within a vulnerability disclosure notice posted on a web page</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be communicated within vulnerability disclosure notice For</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be communicated within vulnerability disclosure notice For"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_7b52d9f5a26671c2" source="e_e163460c91338b08" target="e_55689288f78d350c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be communicated within</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_320cf404a749772f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, this may be communicated within a vulnerability disclosure notice posted on a web page</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be communicated within</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be communicated within"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_e8d325e2b4b8db61" source="e_3caae72f8fe0ae59" target="e_1ba8d72821f0a209"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are precursors to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b36a59df76e29b20</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C11</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, one might describe how certain kinds of SQL Injection vulnerabilities are precursors to a cross-site scripting (XSS) attack, or how a particular kind of buffer overflow would grant local privileges</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are precursors to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are precursors to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_b022352e7f2e58d2" source="e_3caae72f8fe0ae59" target="e_1ba8d72821f0a209"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are how particular kind of buffer overflow to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_67ce6d133e719147</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C11</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, one might describe how certain kinds of SQL Injection vulnerabilities are precursors to a cross-site scripting (XSS) attack, or how a particular kind of buffer overflow would grant local privileges</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are how particular kind of buffer overflow to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are how particular kind of buffer overflow to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_99e397444f87f01b" source="e_3caae72f8fe0ae59" target="e_1f655fbcd62346af"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are how particular kind of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2d779c8bc9b41ce1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C11</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, one might describe how certain kinds of SQL Injection vulnerabilities are precursors to a cross-site scripting (XSS) attack, or how a particular kind of buffer overflow would grant local privileges</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are how particular kind of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are how particular kind of", "describe how particular kind of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_254e9965bb513f1a" source="e_43bf1b4e6e142651" target="e_9f028491fbdc94ee"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">describe how particular kind of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_cc7240e56408f667</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C11</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, one might describe how certain kinds of SQL Injection vulnerabilities are precursors to a cross-site scripting (XSS) attack, or how a particular kind of buffer overflow would grant local privileges</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are how particular kind of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are how particular kind of", "describe how particular kind of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_4fd9fef5e6172691" source="e_74c3188d796f25e9" target="e_f0789276fe127207"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">provides</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_36aaf594b99e9f1b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C11</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Listing the generic types or classes of vulnerabilities provides the minimum information necessary to warn other users, without potentially informing attackers about new exploit opportunities</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">provides</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["provides", "provide"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_e62acdfe35c3d30d" source="e_42b22dca2111584e" target="e_f0789276fe127207"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">provides</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8b6dce757672810b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C11</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Listing the generic types or classes of vulnerabilities provides the minimum information necessary to warn other users, without potentially informing attackers about new exploit opportunities</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">provides</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["provides", "provide"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_4812741a4c7cba42" source="e_2900ed95d90da3e0" target="e_29f374d3ae492bbc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are met such as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a31eac46831ad5df</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C11</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In the event that a vulnerability can be exploited only after other preconditions are met (such as first exploiting another vulnerability), it is acceptable to combine two or more CVSS scores to describe the chain of vulnerabilities by assessing the least-restrictive Exploitability metrics and assessing the most-impactful Impact metrics</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are met such as</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are met such as"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_00ff173d0991d7a4" source="e_c9991551dd8b6f0d" target="e_df8fab3acbb5e0a1"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">uses Exploitability to describe</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f82598adf347b21e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C11</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The following example uses the Exploitability and Impact assessment to describe the chain</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">uses Exploitability to describe</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["uses Exploitability to describe"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_f9554cefd93e7f91" source="e_c9991551dd8b6f0d" target="e_df8fab3acbb5e0a1"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">uses Impact assessment to describe</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_cc397c783ec55cf1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C11</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The following example uses the Exploitability and Impact assessment to describe the chain</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">uses Impact assessment to describe</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["uses Impact assessment to describe"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_35acb50145b16ddb" source="e_c9991551dd8b6f0d" target="e_8deebfd1151914f5"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">uses</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4a4a2bc3d8e22adb</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C11</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The following example uses the Exploitability and Impact assessment to describe the chain</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">use</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["use", "uses", "do use", "Uses"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_f4b9ee701cb7cf2b" source="e_c9991551dd8b6f0d" target="e_b2128d83716c8506"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">uses</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f3ca636a03b86475</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C11</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The following example uses the Exploitability and Impact assessment to describe the chain</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">use</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["use", "uses", "do use", "Uses"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_639fab72e869ffb3" source="e_0499ea7efbd55c2e" target="e_fd55184986b24d5e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">enables attacker to read files on</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_feb8a504f87bb48d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C12</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A vulnerability in a virtual machine that enables an attacker to read and/or delete files on the host operating system (perhaps even its own virtual machine) demonstrates impact to a Subsequent System (the host operating system) as well as to the Vulnerable System (the virtual machine)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">enables attacker to read files on</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["enables attacker to read files on"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_9729670459924225" source="e_0499ea7efbd55c2e" target="e_f03b97bb33e12414"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">enables attacker</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_21758cec48e35c0b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C12</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A vulnerability in a virtual machine that enables an attacker to read and/or delete files on the host operating system (perhaps even its own virtual machine) demonstrates impact to a Subsequent System (the host operating system) as well as to the Vulnerable System (the virtual machine)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">enables attacker</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["enables attacker"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_f406b43bcacc7a19" source="e_00599b254832855a" target="e_546996a8b2a435a8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">demonstrates impact to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3b4f2a2acd71b979</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C12</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A vulnerability in a virtual machine that enables an attacker to read and/or delete files on the host operating system (perhaps even its own virtual machine) demonstrates impact to a Subsequent System (the host operating system) as well as to the Vulnerable System (the virtual machine)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">demonstrates impact to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["demonstrates impact to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_fd0270feac657f4b" source="e_ea8513731f05fb4c" target="e_10f6e726960a586b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be considered when</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_27f4387178c7c05a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C12</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A violation of a security boundary between microprocessor privilege levels should be considered when assessing vulnerabilities using CVSS</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be considered when</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be considered when"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_421dd89915569491" source="e_d123419ce4e3beaa" target="e_eace4ea9596e9c99"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be running in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_823a13dc41bbad76</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C12</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">User space programs’ capabilities running in lower privilege levels are typically limited in what instructions they can run and what registers they can write to even when running under operating system administrator privileges</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be running in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be running in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_a25e1e96a62fcf9d" source="e_290d8da624d84fb0" target="e_8549d517bbb68320"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">write to even when running under</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b8f7637f211430eb</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C12</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">User space programs’ capabilities running in lower privilege levels are typically limited in what instructions they can run and what registers they can write to even when running under operating system administrator privileges</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">write to even when running under</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["write to even when running under"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_19adaaf19409c04c" source="e_f29a5673e5e23112" target="e_10f6e726960a586b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be considered when</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0ab14846fd280189</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C12</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The security boundary between secure enclaves integrated in microprocessors and the rest of operating system processes, including the operating system kernel itself, should be considered when assessing vulnerabilities using CVSS</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be considered when</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be considered when"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_a9ecbaa25e2cd3e0" source="e_017bbd9b23651710" target="e_778160dbe0b1bb41"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">include</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_332c63cc3830419b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C12</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Common vulnerabilities of this type include cross-site scripting and URL redirection</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">include</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["include", "includes"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_95868e897adb3217" source="e_017bbd9b23651710" target="e_807d12a148171d42"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">include</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e8d7f69a24430d64</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C12</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Common vulnerabilities of this type include cross-site scripting and URL redirection</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">include</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["include", "includes"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_15bb9d5d9181cb6b" source="e_7c78e1084fcc7cc8" target="e_3bb18dafe4adc735"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be providing connectivity to components in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_47b094c0a4bdffe4</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In a distributed environment, a vulnerability in a component providing connectivity, protection, or authentication services to components in a different security domain should include assessment for the Subsequent System(s) if a successful attack impacts these other components</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be providing connectivity to components in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be providing connectivity to components in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_27648269396e9aeb" source="e_7c78e1084fcc7cc8" target="e_3bb18dafe4adc735"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be providing protection to components in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_865e086479e22163</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In a distributed environment, a vulnerability in a component providing connectivity, protection, or authentication services to components in a different security domain should include assessment for the Subsequent System(s) if a successful attack impacts these other components</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be providing protection to components in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be providing protection to components in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_d668be61937168c3" source="e_7c78e1084fcc7cc8" target="e_3bb18dafe4adc735"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be providing authentication services to components in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_57537b00a8ca409c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In a distributed environment, a vulnerability in a component providing connectivity, protection, or authentication services to components in a different security domain should include assessment for the Subsequent System(s) if a successful attack impacts these other components</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be providing authentication services to components in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be providing authentication services to components in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_08994aa720e2efbe" source="e_cc91a3d8377e1e6e" target="e_a4daedc7fe22def5"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">include assessment for Subsequent System if</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f45e4159060682f1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In a distributed environment, a vulnerability in a component providing connectivity, protection, or authentication services to components in a different security domain should include assessment for the Subsequent System(s) if a successful attack impacts these other components</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">include assessment for Subsequent System if</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["include assessment for Subsequent System if"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_3bbf294ed28352d4" source="e_ee736e74c5f21c94" target="e_a4daedc7fe22def5"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">include assessment for Subsequent System if</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1bf89730015f939c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In a distributed environment, a vulnerability in a component providing connectivity, protection, or authentication services to components in a different security domain should include assessment for the Subsequent System(s) if a successful attack impacts these other components</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">include assessment for Subsequent System if</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["include assessment for Subsequent System if"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_5e197e2c8a0ef70e" source="e_33a6d55650df3130" target="e_a4daedc7fe22def5"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">include assessment for Subsequent System if</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_75f130f85edfa8a9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In a distributed environment, a vulnerability in a component providing connectivity, protection, or authentication services to components in a different security domain should include assessment for the Subsequent System(s) if a successful attack impacts these other components</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">include assessment for Subsequent System if</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["include assessment for Subsequent System if"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_e64d2c48022e1ef4" source="e_cc91a3d8377e1e6e" target="e_546996a8b2a435a8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">include assessment for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2103d8559890a9c2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In a distributed environment, a vulnerability in a component providing connectivity, protection, or authentication services to components in a different security domain should include assessment for the Subsequent System(s) if a successful attack impacts these other components</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">include assessment for</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["include assessment for"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_0ab6a14032765dc2" source="e_ee736e74c5f21c94" target="e_546996a8b2a435a8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">include assessment for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_10cf56060a60dcc9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In a distributed environment, a vulnerability in a component providing connectivity, protection, or authentication services to components in a different security domain should include assessment for the Subsequent System(s) if a successful attack impacts these other components</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">include assessment for</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["include assessment for"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_7ea608f54cd6f404" source="e_33a6d55650df3130" target="e_546996a8b2a435a8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">include assessment for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d9de1833fd6d541d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In a distributed environment, a vulnerability in a component providing connectivity, protection, or authentication services to components in a different security domain should include assessment for the Subsequent System(s) if a successful attack impacts these other components</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">include assessment for</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["include assessment for"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_497ee65aea9ae416" source="e_c47b9b8ad4cbc4ea" target="e_307218c17d7454bd"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">affects primary availability of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a2dd3529f74ff1d9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, a vulnerability in a component such as a router, firewall, or authentication manager that affects the primary availability of one or more downstream components can impact a Subsequent System</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">affects primary availability of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["affects primary availability of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_394bdf4fb31320b2" source="e_7c78e1084fcc7cc8" target="e_46d56e71076f9b45"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be designed to be deployed as part of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ef914f80c819b7bf</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Additionally, a vulnerability in a component designed to be deployed as part of a larger fault-tolerant topology should not be assessed with a Subsequent System impact if the fault-tolerance means a successful attack does not affect other components</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be designed to be deployed as part of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be designed to be deployed as part of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_a9bb2e679d8dd220" source="e_9e0568711abea57e" target="e_7ee1ff4a70457dd7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be provided by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2aeb7d565e5a19e2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Any effect on additional services provided by the Vulnerable System is considered a secondary impact and not a Subsequent System impact</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be provided by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be provided by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_1787a57425ffc094" source="e_5309f8f497111306" target="e_b35bf6705878f607"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">allows attacker to compromise other files on</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_db00bf0154e39137</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A vulnerability in a simple Portable Document Format (PDF) reader that allows an attacker to compromise other files on the same operating system when a victim opens a malicious PDF document is assessed as having no impact to a Subsequent System</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">allows attacker to compromise other files on</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["allows attacker to compromise other files on"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_20763091edbdff97" source="e_761cc9bc3cf32e49" target="e_b0d5a2d00bf0a58e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are shared between</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b3aa70e8db1afb8a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A SQL injection vulnerability in a web application is not usually considered as causing impact to a Subsequent System assuming that the credentials are shared between web application and impacted SQL database, and therefore they are part of the same security scope</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are shared between</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are shared between"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_56ceb17fe8b59cc0" source="e_290d8da624d84fb0" target="e_c01a240dd22b190d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are part of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5149fe577f0fc6aa</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A SQL injection vulnerability in a web application is not usually considered as causing impact to a Subsequent System assuming that the credentials are shared between web application and impacted SQL database, and therefore they are part of the same security scope</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are part of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are part of", "is part of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_95d99423926f8bb6" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_263de49d43bd1b14"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">crashes</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_acb4227c423380f2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A vulnerability that crashes a web server or SSH server is not considered impact to a Subsequent System since the impact is limited only to the service provided by the affected server</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">crashes</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["crashes"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_290d40b28a9ac274" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_64acae39e69439e5"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">crashes</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0d7009d4c74f9d40</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A vulnerability that crashes a web server or SSH server is not considered impact to a Subsequent System since the impact is limited only to the service provided by the affected server</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">crashes</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["crashes"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_1d4018b3dcc1bfc0" source="e_9ed9f9c2275e8e7e" target="e_265d1c58ed249684"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is limited to service provided by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e7c98d7e5bc8c5a9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A vulnerability that crashes a web server or SSH server is not considered impact to a Subsequent System since the impact is limited only to the service provided by the affected server</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is limited to service provided by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is limited to service provided by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_ee64e49fd6c8b44f" source="e_9111a79bb0a0398b" target="e_265d1c58ed249684"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be provided by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_648efbec91db7db6</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A vulnerability that crashes a web server or SSH server is not considered impact to a Subsequent System since the impact is limited only to the service provided by the affected server</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be provided by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be provided by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_4eabeff931b5928d" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_ac163e65d54540dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">permits attacker to exhaust shared system resource such as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b766b394c98283d2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A vulnerability that permits an attacker to exhaust a shared system resource, such as filling up a file system, should not be considered as causing impact to a Subsequent System</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">permits attacker to exhaust shared system resource such as</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["permits attacker to exhaust shared system resource such as"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_4873db600aeeae10" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_ae88557804e6bd47"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be considered as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_06120fdbd0c5d660</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A vulnerability that permits an attacker to exhaust a shared system resource, such as filling up a file system, should not be considered as causing impact to a Subsequent System</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be considered as</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be considered as"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_bee8b4d18bc79090" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_e9457e2b248d9c8e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is acting under usual capabilities of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2fc98daff343ce86</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The attacker is still acting under the usual capabilities of the application and not breaching any security boundary</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is acting under usual capabilities of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is acting under usual capabilities of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_9ed25431e29fd414" source="e_c4631f903e1159e5" target="e_2c6e3da5d40bff1e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be shared with other components across</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_19f6e92160702e23</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">By exploiting a vulnerability in an application that allows users restricted access to resources shared with other components across multiple security scopes (e.g., operating system resources such as system files), an attacker can access resources that they should not be able to access</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be shared with other components across</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be shared with other components across"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_d199024d26083bce" source="e_290d8da624d84fb0" target="e_f2dca16215b933e8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be able to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b1b835a74c461836</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">By exploiting a vulnerability in an application that allows users restricted access to resources shared with other components across multiple security scopes (e.g., operating system resources such as system files), an attacker can access resources that they should not be able to access</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be able to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be able to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_af984907ea8474f6" source="e_290d8da624d84fb0" target="e_f2dca16215b933e8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be able to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3789cce5e4ff103d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">such as system files), an attacker can access resources that they should not be able to access</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be able to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be able to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_5d99a9ef9df89579" source="e_e9457e2b248d9c8e" target="e_067458e2fc3518b8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">implements</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d6533795b71721fe</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A vulnerability in an application that implements its own security domain which allows attackers to affect resources outside its security scope should be assessed as having Subsequent System impact</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">implement</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["implement", "implements"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_60ab6b986583d3fc" source="e_5d179dc0effbd161" target="e_2c6e3da5d40bff1e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be shared with other components across</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_640f1513c9c958bc</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This assumes the application provides no features for users to access resources governed by a higher-level security domain shared with other components across multiple security scopes (e.g., the resources of the underlying operating system)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be shared with other components across</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be shared with other components across"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_9d6beefacec1f89e" source="e_f6498126c94c6f96" target="e_670573848fbf41cb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">account for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ea09e6e9508f7df8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The analyst should account for the reasonable worst-case scenario</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">account for</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["account for", "accounts for"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_46e7f927ba76ebfb" source="e_4dc239162c062c58" target="e_82307ea50e8b2f0c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">performs</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9c498013d885c3ac</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, a library that performs image conversion would reasonably be used by programs that accept images from untrusted sources over a network</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">perform</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["perform", "performs"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_47992e350b234d1f" source="e_4dc239162c062c58" target="e_e380413965b09830"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_aedb99f8b93f4948</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, a library that performs image conversion would reasonably be used by programs that accept images from untrusted sources over a network</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be used by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be used by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_41f6c5ccd4004692" source="e_e380413965b09830" target="e_28c249862a8f9c3e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">accept images from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_50c71b9b0538814b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, a library that performs image conversion would reasonably be used by programs that accept images from untrusted sources over a network</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">accept images from</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["accept images from"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_a9eed7af742387a9" source="e_e380413965b09830" target="e_2bf2d33645237391"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">accept</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f97a66460cdab5ef</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, a library that performs image conversion would reasonably be used by programs that accept images from untrusted sources over a network</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">accepts</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["accepts", "accept", "accepted"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_80f572a77b6e7f16" source="e_f6498126c94c6f96" target="e_4dc239162c062c58"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be assessing vulnerability in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c0ce45839af4c4c9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As such, an analyst assessing a vulnerability in the library that relates to the incoming data should assume an Attack Vector (AV) of Network (N), but explain this assumption in the summary of the vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be assessing vulnerability in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be assessing vulnerability in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_64fb4cbab5e848c8" source="e_2fa59eb311c8f8b3" target="e_7226ca134696f51b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">relates to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_731f25b5015a4fe1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As such, an analyst assessing a vulnerability in the library that relates to the incoming data should assume an Attack Vector (AV) of Network (N), but explain this assumption in the summary of the vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">relates to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["relates to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_84e1479f73d6a729" source="e_10709c48b24da740" target="e_552292b6b22b985d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">assume Attack Vector of Network As</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0bebabcb076567ca</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As such, an analyst assessing a vulnerability in the library that relates to the incoming data should assume an Attack Vector (AV) of Network (N), but explain this assumption in the summary of the vulnerability</data><data k