tion_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be produced by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be produced by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_7cd22ca4957f86ec" source="e_4801fe47c6613feb" target="e_7b4f67c17e442588"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">change Attack Complexity to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6c9cc3a43da1bcb6</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C15</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">However, a newer operating system has new inherent protection capabilities that change the Attack Complexity to High (H)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">change Attack Complexity to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["change Attack Complexity to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_f4336ff65aafee8d" source="e_4801fe47c6613feb" target="e_76edc2bdd4022652"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">change</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2308b9496fb19814</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C15</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">However, a newer operating system has new inherent protection capabilities that change the Attack Complexity to High (H)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">change</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["change", "changes"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_19ee866512f64673" source="e_ede880f604e26f42" target="e_c0d91b611f395da1"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be outlining</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_778d87a0ce394f03</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C15</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">It is acceptable to assess and publish multiple CVSS-B scores for a single vulnerability provided each has additional language outlining the specific product versions, platforms, and/or operating systems that are relevant to each CVSS-B score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be outlining</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be outlining"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_0dd06b6dbf0ef21e" source="e_ede880f604e26f42" target="e_a71a25fded255343"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be outlining</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a35f0dce3f1a2920</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C15</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">It is acceptable to assess and publish multiple CVSS-B scores for a single vulnerability provided each has additional language outlining the specific product versions, platforms, and/or operating systems that are relevant to each CVSS-B score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be outlining</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be outlining"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_73b8595ddac10d0a" source="e_ede880f604e26f42" target="e_8be38bbecf21a7b3"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be outlining</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_eaccfc35f25cce2a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C15</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">It is acceptable to assess and publish multiple CVSS-B scores for a single vulnerability provided each has additional language outlining the specific product versions, platforms, and/or operating systems that are relevant to each CVSS-B score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be outlining</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be outlining"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_e6a457e919f4d4b1" source="e_afd24f26ffa4591e" target="e_c1f0f9616c9ced1b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">define</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b3b8331087cd1094</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C15</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The following guidelines define a standard method of extending CVSS to include additional metrics and metric groups while retaining the official Base, Threat, and Environmental Metrics</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">define</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["define", "defines"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_240be5b3ab3f039a" source="e_afd24f26ffa4591e" target="e_f33fd9eecdcf9795"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">define</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_23048d830f29d068</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C15</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The following guidelines define a standard method of extending CVSS to include additional metrics and metric groups while retaining the official Base, Threat, and Environmental Metrics</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">define</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["define", "defines"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_014787ae1402a89f" source="e_8e874df517877380" target="e_50b2ccaf2cca5963"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are outside</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8f8ef4364e2c505b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C15</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The additional metrics allow industry sectors such as privacy, safety, automotive, healthcare, etc., to score factors that are outside the core CVSS standard</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are outside</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are outside"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_8d27cc75d5735721" source="e_bbecfad40d527c76" target="e_582cbc3216c9c0c9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be based on</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_cf7194903e481db1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C16</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">New metric groups can be based on existing metric groups</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be based on</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be based on"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_5df19c4ce4e37892" source="e_754fa75553fa09be" target="e_57502fbebac6f4d3"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be based on</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_73c10721546e230d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C16</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The resulting score must be based on adjusting the CVSS-B, CVSS-BT, CVSS-BE, CVSS-BTE scores as appropriate</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be based on</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be based on"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_2e1ca684a9579f2b" source="e_754fa75553fa09be" target="e_fd0e4bf7a89d4789"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be based on</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_228fd3931c750f42</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C16</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The resulting score must be based on adjusting the CVSS-B, CVSS-BT, CVSS-BE, CVSS-BTE scores as appropriate</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be based on</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be based on"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_b483117e9afba512" source="e_754fa75553fa09be" target="e_c3db5f094080754d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be based on</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_25ce6dfd20473605</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C16</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The resulting score must be based on adjusting the CVSS-B, CVSS-BT, CVSS-BE, CVSS-BTE scores as appropriate</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be based on</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be based on"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_24a7b1fe82e56f61" source="e_7e67eadaaf108cde" target="e_6663adf866efaeda"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be listed</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_37aa1cad53cd8ff2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C16</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">CVSS Extension vector strings must be listed separately, utilizing the following format:</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be listed</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be listed"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_bdb70da52fa2f0a3" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_571bc10d653316b8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has choosing over</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e7dbf01b444cae0c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C16</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, a local attacker may be able to trick a vulnerable, privileged, local program into sending sensitive data to a server of the attacker’s choosing over a network</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">has choosing over</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["has choosing over"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_3c3c9296bb650d9b" source="e_b1387b1015bcac9a" target="e_a2d4ff0cca330308"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is required to gather</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_414898cf1f4d98d7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C16</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As a network connection is required to gather the sensitive data this is scored with an Attack Vector of Network</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is required to gather</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is required to gather"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_8f36ff90f7932402" source="e_e163460c91338b08" target="e_955f6f574a1665da"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is scored with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_75f1d3fc08fe8b5c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C16</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As a network connection is required to gather the sensitive data this is scored with an Attack Vector of Network</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is scored with</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is scored with"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_789bc45e0f5f7eef" source="e_340a67b65e9efc13" target="e_9f4bc004f1ab89c0"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is received over network</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3d0432cb28dc765c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C16</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Vulnerabilities where malicious data is received over a network by one system, then passed to a separate system with a vulnerability should be scored with an Attack Vector of Local</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is received over network</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is received over network"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_edc3473590f50483" source="e_3c74f9bc0c3d9897" target="e_da0eaf6d0dc539d1"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">perform system critical actions within</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0d2d156acf0e0a5b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">There could be scenarios where a system user could perform system critical actions, within the user’s own privilege, and then completely deny performing the action; that would cause a Repudiation Impact</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">perform system critical actions</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["perform system critical actions", "perform system critical actions within"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_38fa8336afbd2997" source="e_3c74f9bc0c3d9897" target="e_9ed04b684aeaddcf"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">perform system critical actions</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_92998969924b7b6b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">There could be scenarios where a system user could perform system critical actions, within the user’s own privilege, and then completely deny performing the action; that would cause a Repudiation Impact</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">perform system critical actions</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["perform system critical actions", "perform system critical actions within"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_f333c519a9c53fad" source="e_3c74f9bc0c3d9897" target="e_b330f24574fc9b81"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">deny</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b275f14d13acc94a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">There could be scenarios where a system user could perform system critical actions, within the user’s own privilege, and then completely deny performing the action; that would cause a Repudiation Impact</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">deny</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["deny"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_9e055e4ebd6feeb0" source="e_3c74f9bc0c3d9897" target="e_ba55d6211ac08e71"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">deny</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_25c925e1af75557e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">There could be scenarios where a system user could perform system critical actions, within the user’s own privilege, and then completely deny performing the action; that would cause a Repudiation Impact</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">deny</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["deny"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_a5f784c1c45bdb15" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_3c6c728fe026f9eb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">take malicious actions in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7c4192e702d0e87b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">But the attacker can still take malicious actions in the system by impersonating another user of the same privileges leading to a Repudiation impact, and hence an Integrity impact. (Example: CVE-2017-6785)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">take malicious actions in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["take malicious actions in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_215a033de323bec4" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_966ea6ba0ee45cdd"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">take malicious actions in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6486e503ff1fd05c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">But the attacker can still take malicious actions in the system by impersonating another user of the same privileges leading to a Repudiation impact, and hence an Integrity impact. (Example: CVE-2017-6785)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">take malicious actions in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["take malicious actions in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_eb5e09b66caa7e17" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_93d8650fe6b85a54"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">take malicious actions in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e19257e24298e967</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">But the attacker can still take malicious actions in the system by impersonating another user of the same privileges leading to a Repudiation impact, and hence an Integrity impact. (Example: CVE-2017-6785)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">take malicious actions in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["take malicious actions in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_16703385815477ae" source="e_724a8f4b4b152206" target="e_840d397c0e759c65"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be leading to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_74b0bf055d64342b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">But the attacker can still take malicious actions in the system by impersonating another user of the same privileges leading to a Repudiation impact, and hence an Integrity impact. (Example: CVE-2017-6785)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be leading to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be leading to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_6afe719ee2d6b5f5" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_93d8650fe6b85a54"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">impacts Integrity of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_261959f1e8ba6ef9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Whenever a vulnerability causes a potential repudiation, it immediately impacts the Integrity of the system, along with other subsequent impacts</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">impacts Integrity of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["impacts Integrity of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_76cce5b725c492e4" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_a759ffb9494b80c6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">impacts Integrity of system along with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_094afb17ea551b3a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Whenever a vulnerability causes a potential repudiation, it immediately impacts the Integrity of the system, along with other subsequent impacts</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">impacts Integrity of system along with</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["impacts Integrity of system along with"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_93982eeb0401e64c" source="e_ba0065176e2591f2" target="e_934c1f7b91073d1f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">provides</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d29ccce99dbc5160</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This section provides guidance on selecting appropriate metric values for these based on the characteristics of a specific environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">provides</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["provides", "provide"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_b7689