onal purposes based on regulatory requirements, should be rated High</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be based on</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be based on"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_1359e5983a5b3980" source="e_e1cfc695b1b6dfe7" target="e_7b4f67c17e442588"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be rated</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_548fcdd7f43143b6</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Devices that are required to have rapid response times for transactional purposes based on regulatory requirements, should be rated High</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be rated</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be rated"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_58e6ef3eabcc8fd7" source="e_54b478dcf9b37c22" target="e_1e8070a280814846"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">provides</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e7b17ef218178a00</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A new, optional metric group called the Supplemental metric group provides new metrics that describe and measure additional extrinsic attributes of a vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">provides</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["provides", "provide"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_a4b193139981abf8" source="e_9cf9e67a33f313e5" target="e_d999ddd1227d98cb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be aligned to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2df0653e9ca5563b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When a system has an intended use or fitness of purpose aligned to safety, it is possible that exploiting a vulnerability within that system may have Safety impact which can be represented in the Supplemental Metrics group</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be aligned to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be aligned to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_190fa83b25f9ac53" source="e_fb8ea41b8705c2d6" target="e_8fc389924516130b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be represented in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e77cc6a240fdc11d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When a system has an intended use or fitness of purpose aligned to safety, it is possible that exploiting a vulnerability within that system may have Safety impact which can be represented in the Supplemental Metrics group</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be represented in</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be represented in"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_b3965918e693e010" source="e_022bda0b03ad1169" target="e_3efdc84762bfa93d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">uses</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_09166197fa6cdea3</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">delivery uses channels that widely deployed network security configurations block, and</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">use</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["use", "uses", "do use", "Uses"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_7f244e4c76d793ec" source="e_618d93742ee02dc6" target="e_ad0079b5add58365"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is reliable</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2808f5b3604e06ad</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">exploitation is not reliable, due to exploit-prevention techniques enabled by default; ASLR is an example of an exploit-prevention tool</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is reliable</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is reliable"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_4b921889696145a3" source="e_d517f5dfd7db6dd5" target="e_9299086080c4accc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be enabled by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0a7a37d5857eb6a4</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">exploitation is not reliable, due to exploit-prevention techniques enabled by default; ASLR is an example of an exploit-prevention tool</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be enabled by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be enabled by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_ceaecbfcd574538a" source="e_5cd3d0abe013a8be" target="e_189a4122f3e069ba"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is example of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_dfe1549592815558</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">exploitation is not reliable, due to exploit-prevention techniques enabled by default; ASLR is an example of an exploit-prevention tool</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is example of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is example of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_f295d0f08b217706" source="e_40e9b4cae7572c3e" target="e_fb003243b2adf690"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be provided for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_090c96a4bb21c590</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">These are example reasons, provided for illustration, and are not an exhaustive list of reasons why a kill chain step may not be automatable</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be provided for</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be provided for"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_0508863afb7de770" source="e_970cff862ce2bb64" target="e_fb003243b2adf690"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be provided for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b55939fd3f17fee9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">These are example reasons, provided for illustration, and are not an exhaustive list of reasons why a kill chain step may not be automatable</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be provided for</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be provided for"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_7262bad965971de1" source="e_d4cff6070f136c90" target="e_c1c167f9445786e3"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">provide</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_cb9be086052f982d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Analysts should provide an argument or demonstration that all four steps are able to be automated rather than solely relying on heuristics</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">provides</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["provides", "provide"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_0baf38ba252e5462" source="e_bd446b8be4ff3757" target="e_76f941d8ac2aec07"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">stay</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_94f76756a130a4dd</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The definition of automatable is intended to stay materially the same as the definition of the decision point by the same name in the stakeholder specific vulnerability categorization (version 2)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">stay</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["stay"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_c88a646743ef22b0" source="e_bd446b8be4ff3757" target="e_ebd90615f387a20a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">stay</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a6ff0f1de97a4d4e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The definition of automatable is intended to stay materially the same as the definition of the decision point by the same name in the stakeholder specific vulnerability categorization (version 2)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">stay</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["stay"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_fdfa679d85962003" source="e_bb192ae9e03fa1fb" target="e_4a17d33b79767a98"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be incorporate</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_49426356836d28ff</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">To facilitate a standardized method to incorporate additional provider-supplied assessment, it is proposed to adopt an optional “pass-through” Supplemental Metric called Provider Urgency</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be incorporate</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be incorporate"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_3029053002b74aa7" source="e_62555e79585e1059" target="e_93d8650fe6b85a54"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is responsible for proper operation of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b4465b439f2038db</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C20</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A “system operator” is anyone who is professionally responsible for the proper operation or maintenance of a system.)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is responsible for proper operation of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is responsible for proper operation of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_138b15b24958a782" source="e_62555e79585e1059" target="e_fa752e8a0efa8d52"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is responsible for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_045ee154251485c4</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C20</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A “system operator” is anyone who is professionally responsible for the proper operation or maintenance of a system.)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is responsible for</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is responsible for"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_fb83193428c6a52b" source="e_f46bd6c3e68cd941" target="e_526b5c56fe76dbfd"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are direct responsibility of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_31ed480120836ce1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C20</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Concentrated: Heuristically, such systems are often the direct responsibility of “system operators” rather than users. (A “user” is anyone whose professional task is something other than the maintenance of the system or component</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are direct responsibility of</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are direct responsibility of"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_1f7866d363aaa919" source="e_f46bd6c3e68cd941" target="e_48b9de94f1a079e8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are direct responsibility rather than</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_36ea544e5f7a8c0a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C20</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Concentrated: Heuristically, such systems are often the direct responsibility of “system operators” rather than users. (A “user” is anyone whose professional task is something other than the maintenance of the system or component</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are direct responsibility rather than</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are direct responsibility rather than"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_60c32670258bb690" source="e_403cff0ef11d571d" target="e_bb06948234c7db8a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be hosting</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_957c4ff51e6c76fa</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C20</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A “system operator” is anyone who is professionally responsible for the proper operation or maintenance of a system.) Examples of concentrated value are database systems, Kerberos servers, web servers hosting login pages, and cloud service providers</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be hosting</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be hosting"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_233067251a1bce02" source="e_b513313d2355cbb2" target="e_47869b8b12d1452e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">have concentrated</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_bdeb5a0156e8307e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C20</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, encrypted mobile messaging platforms may have concentrated value, not because each phone’s messaging history has a particularly large amount of data, but because it is uniquely valuable to law enforcement</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">have concentrated</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["have concentrated"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_6e2fa912752d9c83" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_28dd035941535d8c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is valuable to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b492b7ae88214441</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C20</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, encrypted mobile messaging platforms may have concentrated value, not because each phone’s messaging history has a particularly large amount of data, but because it is uniquely valuable to law enforcement</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">is valuable to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["is valuable to"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_42d64ff24595b794" source="e_27c3d83a97913d23" target="e_76f941d8ac2aec07"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">stay</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_257dd1cf0cef3784</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C20</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The definition of value density is intended to stay materially the same as the definition of the decision point by the same name in the stakeholder specific vulnerability categorization (version 2)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">stay</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["stay"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_3a22ebc0115074a0" source="e_27c3d83a97913d23" target="e_ebd90615f387a20a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">stay</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9f11dc3190b45936</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C20</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The definition of value density is intended to stay materially the same as the definition of the decision point by the same name in the stakeholder specific vulnerability categorization (version 2)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">stay</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["stay"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_8bd0f7c15f38e47f" source="e_f7f0082982beecc7" target="e_fd676437ab51b484"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">to provide</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f872f0610ac29057</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C20</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The intention of the Vulnerability Response Effort metric is to provide supplemental information on how difficult it is for consumers to provide an initial response to the impact of vulnerabilities for deployed products and services in their infrastructure</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">to provide</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["to provide"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_359e4e7aa66015a1" source="e_f7f0082982beecc7" target="e_fa83bcbab886e89f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">to provide</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5438549645ccb90a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C20</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The intention of the Vulnerability Response Effort metric is to provide supplemental information on how difficult it is for consumers to provide an initial response to the impact of vulnerabilities for deployed products and services in their infrastructure</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">to provide</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["to provide"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_22dab79834ee38d1" source="e_70973f0fc94d31c9" target="e_7f765772ac6c1cb7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be required into consideration when</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ce4a8f98a936ac99</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C20</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The consumer can then take this additional information on effort required into consideration when applying mitigations and/or scheduling remediation</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be required into consideration when</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be required into consideration when"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_52487c860bc42e4e" source="e_70973f0fc94d31c9" target="e_301ab130bb3a8852"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be required into consideration when</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_88e3ccd5a2ea811f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C20</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The consumer can then take this additional information on effort required into consideration when applying mitigations and/or scheduling remediation</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be required into consideration when</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be required into consideration when"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_1bba0eabfca8dff4" source="e_70973f0fc94d31c9" target="e_d93d3f2293801306"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be required into</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1d9bfdd70db4cf3a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C20</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The consumer can then take this additional information on effort required into consideration when applying mitigations and/or scheduling remediation</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">be required into</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["be required into"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_546f98202dbad602" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_4c69475582351a86"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">use</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9ca833ff7ab62198</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C20</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As much as possible, we will use standard definitions for terms and prefer global, consensus, freely available definitions.4</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">use</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["use", "uses", "do use", "Uses"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_d7587455ca0b7dd9" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_eca0458802e0dd47"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">prefer</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7c41d8ba544e5283</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C20</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As much as possible, we will use standard definitions for terms and prefer global, consensus, freely available definitions.4</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">prefer</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["prefer"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_1fd7ac3b1407b71b" source="e_93d8650fe6b85a54" target="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is affected by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_74009b67b7865b95</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C20</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Affected: A system is affected by a vulnerability if a user or operator of the system must take action to remediate, mitigate, or otherwise address the vulnerability.5 If a system is affected by a vulnerability, the CVSS v4.0 Base score must not be 0.0</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">are affected by</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["are affected by", "is affected by"]</data></edge><edge id="oe_fe11c2e902b4736c" source="e_c7b43ec7e5be0c4a" target="e_6c0b102b5b5a264a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">take action to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_183e966bd684ba31</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C20</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Affected: A system is affected by a vulnerability if a user or operator of the system must take action to remediate, mitigate, or otherwise address the vulnerability.5 If a system is affected by a vulnerability, the CVSS v4.0 Base score must not be 0.0</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data><data key="edge_predicate_canonical">take action to</data><data key="edge_domain">Mention</data><data key="edge_range">Mention</data><data key="edge_derived_from">["take action to"]</data></